COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[205,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nAfter reflecting on the meaning of the deeds that are mentioned in this verse, and grasping them, implement what you can of them.\nGather the verses of allegiance and renunciation, look up their interpretation and refer back to the scholars in order to comprehend more of this subject.\nSupplicate Allah to give you forbearance, and make it a habit so that it becomes a quality of yours.\nguid\nThe rite of enjoining what is right and forbidding what is evil, is of a great importance, but have we grasped this fact yet?\nThe reality of faith necessitates giving precedence to the believer, even if he is distantly related, and putting the disbeliever last, even if he is a close family member.\nObeying Allah in what the soul considers hardship is one of the reasons of Allah's acceptance of the servant's repentance.\nrefl\nٱلتَّٰٓئِبُونَ ٱلۡعَٰبِدُونَ ٱلۡحَٰمِدُونَ ٱلسَّٰٓئِحُونَ ٱلرَّٰكِعُونَ ٱلسَّٰجِدُونَ ٱلۡأٓمِرُونَ بِٱلۡمَعۡرُوفِ وَٱلنَّاهُونَ عَنِ ٱلۡمُنكَرِ وَٱلۡحَٰفِظُونَ لِحُدُودِ ٱللَّهِۗ\n(The worshipers), that is, their attribute is servitude to Allah and constantly obeying Him by doing obligatory and recommended acts oftentimes. When doing that, a servant becomes one of those worshipers. Al-Saadi: 353.\nWhen can a person be described as a worshiper?\nوَبَشِّرِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ١١٢\nNo mention is made of what the glad tidings refer to; hence, it includes every reward in this world and the Hereafter which results from faith. The glad tidings are applicable to every believer, but its magnitude and description are commensurate with the strength and weakness of their faith and their adherence thereto. Al-Saadi: 353.\nAllah does not mention what the glad tidings refer to. Why?\nمَا كَانَ لِلنَّبِيِّ وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ أَن يَسۡتَغۡفِرُواْ لِلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ وَلَوۡ كَانُوٓاْ أُوْلِي قُرۡبَىٰ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمۡ أَنَّهُمۡ أَصۡحَٰبُ ٱلۡجَحِيمِ ١١٣\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) and those who believed with him are required to go along with their Lord with regard to what pleases or angers Him, and to take as allies those whom Allah takes as allies, as well as take as enemies those whom Allah takes as enemies. So, their praying for forgiveness for one who is clearly doomed to Hellfire is contrary to that. Al-Saadi: 353.\nIn light of this verse, explain a bit about the belief of allegiance and renunciation.\nوَمَا لَكُم مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ مِن وَلِيّٖ وَلَا نَصِيرٖ ١١٦\nSince one may be helped by other than his relatives, Allah says, (and you have not besides Allah any protector or any helper), that is, do not take an ally except among Allah's party and those whom He loves. This is a threat to anyone who becomes friendly with the enemies of Allah, either openly or in secret, to eventually gain their alliance which will not avail them against Allah. Al-Biqai: 3/395.\nThis verse is indicative of the allegiance and renunciation for the sake of Allah only. Explain.\nلَّقَد تَّابَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَى ٱلنَّبِيِّ وَٱلۡمُهَٰجِرِينَ وَٱلۡأَنصَارِ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّبَعُوهُ فِي سَاعَةِ ٱلۡعُسۡرَةِ\nAllah calls it (the hour) to ease the times of hardships, and to encourage them to face these hardships since they do not last long but their reward is great. Al-Biqai: 3/396.\nThere is a useful lesson in this verse, (the hour of hardship). Explain.\nلَّقَد تَّابَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَى ٱلنَّبِيِّ وَٱلۡمُهَٰجِرِينَ وَٱلۡأَنصَارِ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّبَعُوهُ فِي سَاعَةِ ٱلۡعُسۡرَةِ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا كَادَ يَزِيغُ قُلُوبُ فَرِيقٖ مِّنۡهُمۡ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيۡهِمۡۚ إِنَّهُۥ بِهِمۡ رَءُوفٞ رَّحِيمٞ ١١٧\nIf it is said, why is the mention of (turned in mercy) repeated twice in this verse? The answer is that the first mention comes before the reference to the sin, and when the sin is referenced, Allah repeats (turned to them in mercy) to indicate His acceptance of their repentance. Al-Baghawi: 2/336.\nWhat is wisdom behind repeating the mention of (turned in mercy) in the verse?\nلَّقَد تَّابَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَى ٱلنَّبِيِّ وَٱلۡمُهَٰجِرِينَ وَٱلۡأَنصَارِ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّبَعُوهُ فِي سَاعَةِ ٱلۡعُسۡرَةِ\nThe hardships were the combination of shortage of rides, food and water. Al-Qurtubi: 10/407.\nWhat was the extent of the hardships faced by the Prophet's (ﷺ) Companions at Tabuk expedition?\nwords\nالسَّائِحُونَThose who fast\nسَاعَةِ العُسرَةِThe time of hardship [at Tabuk expedition]\nيَزِيغُLoses heart [deviates]"],[206,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nRead the Hadith of Ka'b ibn Malik (t) about staying behind in the battle of Tabuk from one of Sunna or history books, then draw five lessons from that.\nBecome closer to Allah by repenting from a sin.\nWhile pursuing or participating in a good deed, remember that all of your steps are recorded for you.\nguid\nA truthful repentant may be tested for his truthfulness and steadfastness.\nEach person is enabled to do that for which he has been created. If you are qualified to acquire knowledge, do not let worldly things distract you.\nOne of the tasks of students and scholars is to warn their people.\nrefl\nوَعَلَى ٱلثَّلَٰثَةِ ٱلَّذِينَ خُلِّفُواْ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا ضَاقَتۡ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡأَرۡضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتۡ وَضَاقَتۡ عَلَيۡهِمۡ أَنفُسُهُمۡ وَظَنُّوٓاْ أَن لَّا مَلۡجَأَ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ إِلَّآ إِلَيۡهِ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيۡهِمۡ لِيَتُوبُوٓاْۚ\nAllah's turning in mercy toward His servant is commensurate with his remorse and great regret. If a person does not care about sin and does not feel any shame if he does it, then there is doubt as to whether his repentance is accepted, even if he claims that it is acceptable. Al-Saadi: 354.\nThis verse points to an important pillar of repentance. What is it?\nوَعَلَى ٱلثَّلَٰثَةِ ٱلَّذِينَ خُلِّفُواْ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا ضَاقَتۡ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡأَرۡضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتۡ وَضَاقَتۡ عَلَيۡهِمۡ أَنفُسُهُمۡ وَظَنُّوٓاْ أَن لَّا مَلۡجَأَ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ إِلَّآ إِلَيۡهِ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيۡهِمۡ لِيَتُوبُوٓاْۚ\nThe sign of relief and the end of hardship is when a person puts his hope completely in Allah and abandons hope in all created beings. Al-Saadi: 354.\nWhen does relief come to a person in hardship?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَكُونُواْ مَعَ ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ ١١٩\nPerhaps this verse means telling the truth since the three Companions who were left alone told the truth and did not lie with false excuses, so, Allah rewarded them. Or, perhaps it means the believers should be truthful in general with their words, actions, intentions and resolves. Ibn Juzay: 1/372.\nTruthfulness is a great trait since it encompasses more than a single meaning. Explain.\nذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمۡ لَا يُصِيبُهُمۡ ظَمَأٞ وَلَا نَصَبٞ وَلَا مَخۡمَصَةٞ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ وَلَا يَطَـُٔونَ مَوۡطِئٗا يَغِيظُ ٱلۡكُفَّارَ وَلَا يَنَالُونَ مِنۡ عَدُوّٖ نَّيۡلًا إِلَّا كُتِبَ لَهُم بِهِۦ عَمَلٞ صَٰلِحٌۚ\nAllah, the Almighty, rewards the servant for the hardship that comes while doing good deeds, as He says, (That is because whenever they suffer any thirst...). The Prophet (ﷺ) said to Aisha (i):\"Your reward will be commensurate with your hardship.\" Ibn Taimyah: 3/461.\nThe Muslim will receive a reward for his deed and hardship. Explain in light of this verse.\nلِّيَتَفَقَّهُواْ فِي ٱلدِّينِ وَلِيُنذِرُواْ قَوۡمَهُمۡ إِذَا رَجَعُوٓاْ إِلَيۡهِمۡ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَحۡذَرُونَ ١٢٢\nAllah makes clear that the objective of knowledge is to have fear of Him as indicated by (they might), which means all of them, and (might be cautious) so they become fearful of Allah because of the Fiqh they earned since it is the basis of all good. Their hearts become clear, and they pursue good deeds and refrain from evil. Fiqh is defined here as learning the Quran and Sunnah, as well as grasping their fundamentals, branches, etiquettes and virtues. Al-Biqai: 3/403.\nWhat do you think of one who has knowledge but does not fear Allah Almighty?\nوَمَا كَانَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ لِيَنفِرُواْ كَآفَّةٗۚ فَلَوۡلَا نَفَرَ مِن كُلِّ فِرۡقَةٖ مِّنۡهُمۡ طَآئِفَةٞ لِّيَتَفَقَّهُواْ فِي ٱلدِّينِ وَلِيُنذِرُواْ قَوۡمَهُمۡ إِذَا رَجَعُوٓاْ إِلَيۡهِمۡ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَحۡذَرُونَ ١٢٢\nThis verse also offers a proof, guidance and a subtle recommendation that may serve a great interest, which is that Muslims should appoint for each of their public interests someone who would take care of it, devote his time to it, work hard at it, and will not be distracted by other activities. Thus, all public interests will be taken care of and their benefits will be harnessed, and they will all be striving together to achieve one purpose, which is taking care of that which will fulfill their religious and worldly interests; even if everyone has a different role and a different approach. The actions may be different but the aim is one. This is a wise approach that helps to achieve all aims. Al-Saadi: 355.\nThis verse forms a basis for the science of business administration. Explain.\nوَمَا كَانَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ لِيَنفِرُواْ كَآفَّةٗۚ فَلَوۡلَا نَفَرَ مِن كُلِّ فِرۡقَةٖ مِّنۡهُمۡ طَآئِفَةٞ لِّيَتَفَقَّهُواْ فِي ٱلدِّينِ وَلِيُنذِرُواْ قَوۡمَهُمۡ إِذَا رَجَعُوٓاْ إِلَيۡهِمۡ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَحۡذَرُونَ ١٢٢\nWhoever acquires knowledge should share and spread it among people, and he should be sincere toward them in doing so, for the spread of knowledge by a knowledgeable person will bring him blessing and reward that will grow for him. However, if he keeps that knowledge to himself, does not call people to the path of Allah with wisdom and good exhortation and fails to teach the ignorant what they need to know, then what benefit will that bring to the Muslims? What result will come from his knowledge? Ultimately, he will die, and his knowledge and the benefits thereof will die with him. Moreover, this is the utmost deprivation for one to whom Allah has granted the blessing of knowledge and understanding. Al-Saadi: 355.\nWhat is the ideal way for a knowledgeable person to benefit others with his knowledge?\nwords\nبِمَا رَحُبَتIn spite of its vastness\nمَخمَصَةٌHunger\nنَيلًا قَتلًاKilling, defeat or affliction"],[207,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nWhenever you feel weakness in your faith today, recite some of the verses of the Quran with the intention to increase your faith.\nSay, \"O Allah, Controller of the hearts, direct my heart to Your obedience and love.\"\nSay, \"Sufficient for me is Allah; there is no deity except Him. On Him I have relied, and He is the Lord of the Great Throne.\"\nguid\nIf you want to attain the company of Allah, fear Him by making His command precede your whim.\nIf you find that your heart is not benefiting from the Quran, then know that it has sickness.\nThis verse mentions four traits of the Prophet (ﷺ). Identify them, and try to emulate them.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ قَٰتِلُواْ ٱلَّذِينَ يَلُونَكُم مِّنَ ٱلۡكُفَّارِ وَلۡيَجِدُواْ فِيكُمۡ غِلۡظَةٗۚ\nThe complete believer is he who is kind to his believing brother, and harsh with his disbelieving enemy. Ibn Kathir: 2/384.\nHow should the believer deal with his believing brother, and with the disbelieving enemy?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ قَٰتِلُواْ ٱلَّذِينَ يَلُونَكُم مِّنَ ٱلۡكُفَّارِ وَلۡيَجِدُواْ فِيكُمۡ غِلۡظَةٗۚ\nThe aim of being harsh is to cast terror into the hearts of enemies so that they would fear the consequence of fighting the Muslims. Ibn Ashur: 11/63.\nWhat is the aim of commanding Muslim fighters to deal harshly with the polytheists?\nوَإِذَا مَآ أُنزِلَتۡ سُورَةٞ فَمِنۡهُم مَّن يَقُولُ أَيُّكُمۡ زَادَتۡهُ هَٰذِهِۦٓ إِيمَٰنٗاۚ فَأَمَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ فَزَادَتۡهُمۡ إِيمَٰنٗا وَهُمۡ يَسۡتَبۡشِرُونَ ١٢٤ وَأَمَّا ٱلَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٞ فَزَادَتۡهُمۡ رِجۡسًا إِلَىٰ رِجۡسِهِمۡ\nSome of the hypocrites used to ridicule the Quran by saying to each other: \"Which of you has this increased in faith,\" as saying, \"What is so special about this?\" Or, \"What does this prove?\" (As for those who believed, it has increased them in faith), because, to them, the proofs are renewed with every revealed Surah. (But as for those in whose hearts is sickness, it only increases them in wickedness to their wickedness) that it, increases them in disbelief and hypocrisy in addition to their disbelief and hypocrisy. Ibn Juzay: 1/374.\nThe revelation of a verse can increase the faith of some and the hypocrisy of others. How?\nأَوَلَا يَرَوۡنَ أَنَّهُمۡ يُفۡتَنُونَ فِي كُلِّ عَامٖ مَّرَّةً أَوۡ مَرَّتَيۡنِ ثُمَّ لَا يَتُوبُونَ وَلَا هُمۡ يَذَّكَّرُونَ ١٢٦\nThere is no doubt that the trial, mentioned in this verse, applies exclusively to the hypocrites. These trials can be diseases, loss of wealth, destroyed crops or loss of their lives or that of their loved ones. When two of these hardships occurred in a year, it indicates that they have been tried twice. Ibn Ashur: 11/67.\nWhat is meant by the trial in this verse?\nلَقَدۡ جَآءَكُمۡ رَسُولٞ مِّنۡ أَنفُسِكُمۡ عَزِيزٌ عَلَيۡهِ مَا عَنِتُّمۡ حَرِيصٌ عَلَيۡكُم بِٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ رَءُوفٞ رَّحِيمٞ ١٢٨\n(And is concerned for you), the Messenger loves that which is good for you, strives his utmost to achieve it for you, and is very keen that you are guided to faith. He hates for you to follow evil and strives to turn you away from it. (And is gracious and merciful towards the believers), he is extremely kind to them, and is more compassionate toward them than their parents. Al-Saadi: 357.\nWhat are the traits that make a preacher to Allah accepted by people?\nلَقَدۡ جَآءَكُمۡ رَسُولٞ مِّنۡ أَنفُسِكُمۡ عَزِيزٌ عَلَيۡهِ مَا عَنِتُّمۡ حَرِيصٌ عَلَيۡكُم بِٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ رَءُوفٞ رَّحِيمٞ ١٢٨\n(And is concerned for you), he cares about your faith and contentment. (And is gracious and merciful towards the believers), here, Allah calls His Prophet (ﷺ) by two of His Names. Ibn Juzay: 1/374.\nThe love of Allah induces some traits upon His servant. Give an example from this verse.\nفَإِن تَوَلَّوۡاْ فَقُلۡ حَسۡبِيَ ٱللَّهُ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَۖ عَلَيۡهِ تَوَكَّلۡتُۖ وَهُوَ رَبُّ ٱلۡعَرۡشِ ٱلۡعَظِيمِ ١٢٩\nThis verse commends this blessed invocation because the Prophet (ﷺ) is commanded to say these exact words in addition to relying on Allah. Ibn Ashur: 11/74.\nThis blessed invocation is commended in this verse. Why?\nwords\nيَلُونَكُمThose who are around you\nمَرَضٌDoubt and hypocrisy\nرِجسًاHypocrisy and doubt\nيُفتَنُونَThe are tried by drought, hardship and the exposure of their hypocrisy\nعَزِيزٌDifficult and hard\nمَا عَنِتُّمYour suffering and hardship"],[208,"§Yunus\ndeeds\nSend a message to one who calls others to Allah, in which you give him glad tidings that his steadfastness in his work is a sign of truthfulness.\nSay, \"O Allah, I ask You to grant me the intercession of You Prophet(ﷺ).\"\nLearn some subjects in astronomy because it enhances faith.\nguid\nThis is the glad tidings of what Allah has prepared for those who believe and do righteous deeds.\nThe disbelievers will never cease to lie or misguide.\nDo not ask a living or dead person to intercede on your behalf on the Last Day, rather ask the One Whom no one can intercede except by His permission.\nrefl\nالٓرۚ تِلۡكَ ءَايَٰتُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ ٱلۡحَكِيمِ ١\nThe link between the conclusion of Surat At-Tawbah and the beginning of this Surah is made clear in these two points: The preceding Surah concludes with the mention of the Messenger (ﷺ), and this Surah begins with that too. The preceding Surah mentions what the hypocrites say when a Surah of the Quran is revealed, and this Surah mentions what the disbelievers say about the Quran. Al-Alusi: 11/79.\nWhat is the link between the conclusion of Surat At-Tawbah and the beginning of Surat Yunus?\nإِنَّ رَبَّكُمُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِي خَلَقَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضَ فِي سِتَّةِ أَيَّامٖ\nEven though He is able to create them in a single moment but He did not, because of His divine wisdom and the Graciousness of His actions. Al-Saadi: 357.\nWhy did Allah not create Heavens and earth in a single moment?\nمَا مِن شَفِيعٍ إِلَّا مِنۢ بَعۡدِ إِذۡنِهِۦۚ ذَٰلِكُمُ ٱللَّهُ رَبُّكُمۡ فَٱعۡبُدُوهُۚ أَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُونَ ٣\nSo, none of them can come forward to intercede, even if he is the best of creation, until Allah grants permission. He does not grant permission to anyone except one with whom He is pleased, and He is not pleased with anyone except those who are sincere to Him alone and affirm His Oneness. Al-Saadi: 357.\nWhat are the two conditions for intercession?\nإِنَّهُۥ يَبۡدَؤُاْ ٱلۡخَلۡقَ ثُمَّ يُعِيدُهُۥ لِيَجۡزِيَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ بِٱلۡقِسۡطِۚ\nJustly): Fairly. This is to explain the rationale of life after death, since this worldly life is for doing deeds while the recompense for these deeds is in the Hereafter, and that is why the resurrection is deemed necessary and certain. Al-Jaza'iri : 2/448.\nWhat is the wisdom behind resurrecting people after death?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ لَهُمۡ شَرَابٞ مِّنۡ حَمِيمٖ وَعَذَابٌ أَلِيمُۢ بِمَا كَانُواْ يَكۡفُرُونَ ٤\nAmong all painful torment, drinking scalding water is singled out for mention because it is the most abhorred torment to the souls. Ibn Ashur: 11/93.\nWhy is drinking scalding water is singled out for mention?\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِي جَعَلَ ٱلشَّمۡسَ ضِيَآءٗ وَٱلۡقَمَرَ نُورٗا وَقَدَّرَهُۥ مَنَازِلَ لِتَعۡلَمُواْ عَدَدَ ٱلسِّنِينَ وَٱلۡحِسَابَۚ مَا خَلَقَ ٱللَّهُ ذَٰلِكَ إِلَّا بِٱلۡحَقِّۚ يُفَصِّلُ ٱلۡأٓيَٰتِ لِقَوۡمٖ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٥ إِنَّ فِي ٱخۡتِلَٰفِ ٱلَّيۡلِ وَٱلنَّهَارِ وَمَا خَلَقَ ٱللَّهُ فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَتَّقُونَ ٦\nThese verses urge and encourage us to reflect on the creations of Allah, to examine them and seek to learn lessons from them. Thus, our insight will deepen, our faith and knowledge will increase, and reason will be strengthened. However, neglecting that implies that one is taking this command of Allah lightly, which closes the door to any increase in faith and causes the mind to stagnate. Al-Saadi: 358.\nWhy is it important to reflect of the creations of Allah?\nإِنَّ فِي ٱخۡتِلَٰفِ ٱلَّيۡلِ وَٱلنَّهَارِ وَمَا خَلَقَ ٱللَّهُ فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَتَّقُونَ ٦\n(There are signs for people who fear Him), those who fear Allah are singled out for mention because fear of Allah stimulates reflection and pondering. Al-Alusi: 11/97.\nWhich trait that stimulates reflection and pondering?\nwords\nقَدَمَ صِدقٍA great reward for their righteous deeds\nاستَوَى عَلَى العَرشِHe rose over the Throne in a manner that suits His Majesty\nبِالقِسطِWith justice\nحَمِيمٍA scalding water, heated to the utmost degree\nوَقَدَّرَهُ مَنَازِلَHe determined the phases of the moon\nاختِلاَفِAlternation"],[209,"§Yunus\ndeeds\nListen to an admonishment to remind you of the Hereafter.\nPraise Allah, the Lord of the worlds, after concluding every good deed today.\nRecall, today, a hardship or a disease from which Allah relieved you, and strive in praising and thanking Him.\nguid\nIgnoring the Hereafter is the beginning of heedlessness.\nDo not be heedless of what is transpiring around you such as news, events and disasters because all of that serve as a reminder to you.\nFaith is a reason for guidance from Allah. Strive to increase your faith so that Allah increases you in guidance.\nrefl\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يَرۡجُونَ لِقَآءَنَا وَرَضُواْ بِٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَٱطۡمَأَنُّواْ بِهَا وَٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ عَنۡ ءَايَٰتِنَا غَٰفِلُونَ ٧ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ مَأۡوَىٰهُمُ ٱلنَّارُ بِمَا كَانُواْ يَكۡسِبُونَ ٨\nAl-Hasan said: \"They adorned it and praised it until they were well pleased with it. Whereas they were heedless of Allah's signs in the universe, they did not contemplate them. They were also heedless of Allah's laws, for they did not abide by them. Their abode on the Day of Return is Fire, a recompense for the sins and crimes which they have earned in their worldly life.\" Ibn Kathir: 2/389.\nState one of the signs of contentment with the life of this world.\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يَرۡجُونَ لِقَآءَنَا وَرَضُواْ بِٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَٱطۡمَأَنُّواْ بِهَا وَٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ عَنۡ ءَايَٰتِنَا غَٰفِلُونَ\n(And are pleased and content with the life of this world), they inclined to it and made it their ultimate goal and aspiration. Thus, they strive for it and focus on its pleasures and desires, regardless of how they attain them. Moreover, whatever opportunities they come across, they rush to seize them and focus their thoughts, intentions, ideas and deeds on attaining them. (And those who are heedless of Our signs), so they do not benefit from the verses of the Quran, or the signs in the universe or in their own selves. Turning away from evidence implies turning away from and neglecting that to which it points. Al-Saadi: 358.\nThe verse mentions an obstacle to benefiting from the verses of the Quran. What is it?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ يَهۡدِيهِمۡ رَبُّهُم بِإِيمَٰنِهِمۡۖ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهِمُ ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُ فِي جَنَّٰتِ ٱلنَّعِيمِ ٩\n(Their Lord will guide them by virtue of their faith) Allah makes them steadfast and guide them to the straight path in this life, or shows them the way to Paradise in the Hereafter. Ibn Juzay: 1/376.\nIn light of this verse, what is the end result of faith?\nفِي جَنَّٰتِ ٱلنَّعِيمِ ٩\nAllah describes the Gardens as such because they contain the perfect Bliss, filling the heart with joy, happiness and cheerfulness; the joy of seeing the Most Gracious and hearing His words, and of attaining His good pleasure and being close to Him; the joy of meeting loved ones and brothers and enjoying their company; listening to delightful voices and pleasant tunes; gazing upon joyful scenes; physical pleasures such as all kinds of food and drinks, and intimacy with spouses; and other things such as no one knows and has never crossed the mind of anyone, indescribable pleasures. Al-Saadi: 359.\nThe Gardens are described as \"the Gardens of Bliss,\" why?\nدَعۡوَىٰهُمۡ فِيهَا سُبۡحَٰنَكَ ٱللَّهُمَّ وَتَحِيَّتُهُمۡ فِيهَا سَلَٰمٞۚ وَءَاخِرُ دَعۡوَىٰهُمۡ أَنِ ٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ١٠\nAll duties will be waived from them in the realm of reward, and all that will be left for them will be the most perfect of pleasures, one that is greater than delicious food, namely remembrance of Allah in which hearts find rest and souls feel joy. For them it will be like breathing without any effort or difficulty. Al-Saadi: 359.\nIt is well known that duties will be waived for people on the Day of Judgment. Then, how will they perform these acts of worship?\nوَإِذَا مَسَّ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ ٱلضُّرُّ دَعَانَا لِجَنۢبِهِۦٓ أَوۡ قَاعِدًا أَوۡ قَآئِمٗا فَلَمَّا كَشَفۡنَا عَنۡهُ ضُرَّهُۥ مَرَّ كَأَن لَّمۡ يَدۡعُنَآ إِلَىٰ ضُرّٖ مَّسَّهُۥۚ\nIn this verse, there is a rebuke to those who neglect supplicating Allah during the times of comfort, but rush to supplicate Him during the times of hardship. The proper attitude of the complete believer is to humble himself to his Lord during the times of comfort and hardship, for his supplication is more likely to be answered. In one Prophetic Hadith: \"Remember Allah in times of ease and prosperity, and He will remember you in times of adversity.\" Al-Alusi: 11/108\nThis verse states some of the etiquettes of supplication. What are they?\nكَذَٰلِكَ زُيِّنَ لِلۡمُسۡرِفِينَ مَا كَانُواْ يَعۡمَلُونَ ١٢\n(The misdeeds), they turned away from remembering and invoking Allah; and became absorbed in lustful desires and excessiveness. They are called transgressors because when Allah gave them the powers and sensibilities to use them in what they are intended for such as gaining knowledge and doing good deeds, they used them for useless aims instead. Al-Alusi: 11/108.\nTransgression can be done in spending wealth, and it can be more general than that. Explain the broader meaning of transgression.\nwords\nدَعوَاهُمTheir prayer (supplication)\nيَعمَهُونَThey wander with hesitation\nلِجَنبِهِHe is lying on his side\nمَرَّ استَمَرَّHe continues in his disbelief\nالقُرُونَThe denying nations\nخَلاَئِفَWe made you successors"],[210,"§Yunus\ndeeds\nRecall a major sin that you had committed, then ask much for Allah’s forgiveness, and do more good deeds, so that Allah may forgive you.\nWarn those around you against shirk, and explain to them that invoking other than Allah or asking for the intercession of the dead is indeed shirk.\nShare a message in which you explain the importance of unity and casting aside the disunity and differences.\nguid\nCombining the lack of fear of Allah with committing sins is a sign of a sick heart.\nThe constant reminding of the Hereafter protects one from falling into sins.\nHad the Quran not been revealed, we would have been among the most ignorant; therefore, let us honor and observe the rulings of this great Book.\nrefl\nوَإِذَا تُتۡلَىٰ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ءَايَاتُنَا بَيِّنَٰتٖ قَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يَرۡجُونَ لِقَآءَنَا ٱئۡتِ بِقُرۡءَانٍ غَيۡرِ هَٰذَآ أَوۡ بَدِّلۡهُۚ قُلۡ مَا يَكُونُ لِيٓ أَنۡ أُبَدِّلَهُۥ مِن تِلۡقَآيِٕ نَفۡسِيٓۖ إِنۡ أَتَّبِعُ إِلَّا مَا يُوحَىٰٓ إِلَيَّۖ إِنِّيٓ أَخَافُ إِنۡ عَصَيۡتُ رَبِّي عَذَابَ يَوۡمٍ عَظِيمٖ ١٥\nThe change they were asking for was to replace a verse of a threat with another of a promise, and replace a verse of a promise with another of a threat. Moreover, they asked, to change the unlawful to lawful, and the lawful to unlawful; hence, Allah commands His Prophet (ﷺ) to inform them that it is not for him to do that, rather, it is up to the One Whose judgment cannot be overturned, nor His decree be contested. The Prophet (ﷺ) is no more than a conveying Messenger and an obedient follower. Al-Tabari: 15/40.\nExplain the risk in changing the rules of Sharia in accordance with whims and self-interests.\nقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يَرۡجُونَ لِقَآءَنَا ٱئۡتِ بِقُرۡءَانٍ غَيۡرِ هَٰذَآ أَوۡ بَدِّلۡهُۚ\nIf they claim that their aim is for the truth to become evident by means of the signs that they demanded, then they are lying, for Allah has already shown them signs on the basis of which people have believed. Moreover, He is the One Who sends signs as He wills in accordance with His divine wisdom and mercy toward His servants. Al-Saadi: 360.\nThe dialogue does not benefit anyone unless it is truthful. Explain in light of this verse.\nقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يَرۡجُونَ لِقَآءَنَا\n(Those who do not expect to meet Us say) this indicates that what prompted them to be so stubborn was their lack of belief in meeting Allah or expecting to meet Him. The one who expects to meet Allah will inevitably submit to this Book and believe in it, for his intention is good. Al-Saadi: 360.\nWhat is the reason for the obstinacy of hypocrites and disbelievers toward Islamic issues?\nفَقَدۡ لَبِثۡتُ فِيكُمۡ عُمُرٗا مِّن قَبۡلِهِۦٓۚ\n(For I had remained among you a lifetime before it), I spent my whole life among you, and you know me well; you know that I am unlettered and can neither read nor write, and I have not studied or learned from anyone, but I have brought you this great Book that the most eloquent and knowledgeable of people are unable to match. As that is the case, how could I have produced it of my own accord? Is this not a definitive proof that it is a revelation from the Most Wise, Worthy of all praise? If you think on the basis of reason and understanding, and you reflect on my situation and that of this Book, you will reach a level of certainty far beyond any doubt that it is the truth beyond which is nothing but misguidance. However, if you insist on stubbornly disbelieving, then undoubtedly you are wrongdoers. Al-Saadi: 360.\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) told his people that he spent a lifetime with them before. Why?\nوَيَعۡبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ مَا لَا يَضُرُّهُمۡ وَلَا يَنفَعُهُمۡ وَيَقُولُونَ هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ شُفَعَٰٓؤُنَا عِندَ ٱللَّهِۚ\nThey admitted that their gods did not join Allah in creating heavens and earth, nor anything else, rather they were considering them as intercessors and mediators, as Allah says, (And they worship other than Allah that which neither harms them nor benefits them, and they say, \"These are our intercessors with Allah\"). Ibn Taimyah: 3/473.\nIn light of this verse, how do you respond to a grave worshiper who says: I only seek their intercession?\nوَيَقُولُونَ لَوۡلَآ أُنزِلَ عَلَيۡهِ ءَايَةٞ مِّن رَّبِّهِۦۖ فَقُلۡ إِنَّمَا ٱلۡغَيۡبُ لِلَّهِ فَٱنتَظِرُوٓاْ إِنِّي مَعَكُم مِّنَ ٱلۡمُنتَظِرِينَ ٢٠\nMeaning: Say, you asked me for the unseen, which belongs only to Allah. No one knows why He did not do that, but He only knows. Al-Baghawi: 2/356\nSome TV channel broadcasters claim that they know the unseen and can find the lost. What should the belief of the believer toward these claims?\nوَيَقُولُونَ لَوۡلَآ أُنزِلَ عَلَيۡهِ ءَايَةٞ مِّن رَّبِّهِۦۖ فَقُلۡ إِنَّمَا ٱلۡغَيۡبُ لِلَّهِ فَٱنتَظِرُوٓاْ إِنِّي مَعَكُم مِّنَ ٱلۡمُنتَظِرِينَ ٢٠\nIf they were seeking the guidance and firm knowledge by asking for signs, Allah would have known that and would have granted them what they requested. But Allah knew that it was their obstinacy that was behind their request; therefore, He left them to suffer in their suspicion and doubt. Ibn Kathir: 2/394.\nAllah did not grant the polytheists the signs to prove that Muhammad (ﷺ) speaks the truth. Why?\nwords\nتِلقَاءِ نَفسِيFrom my own self\nأَدرَاكُمHe had made it known to you"],[211,"§Yunus\ndeeds\nRecall a distress that you had encountered, then thank Allah that He rescued you from it, and do not be among the heedless.\nRecall a promise you made with Allah but you did not keep, and go fulfill it now.\nAsk Allah to grant you the Home of Peace.\nguid\nExperiencing comfort after distress induces heedlessness and further distance from Allah, the Almighty, except for a cautious one.\nDo not forget that everything you say or do is recorded, and you will be recompensed for it on the Day of Resurrection.\nBe aware that every injustice or wrongdoing you commit, the consequence of which will befall you.\nrefl\nوَإِذَآ أَذَقۡنَا ٱلنَّاسَ رَحۡمَةٗ مِّنۢ بَعۡدِ ضَرَّآءَ مَسَّتۡهُمۡ إِذَا لَهُم مَّكۡرٞ فِيٓ ءَايَاتِنَاۚ\nThis verse demonstrates some of the etiquettes of the Quran, where it expresses causing adversity as (touched), while it attributes the taste of mercy to the holy pronoun of Allah: “We”. This is similar to His saying: (And when I am ill, it is He Who cures me) [26:80], and in other instances in the Quran. Hence, this etiquette should be observed, as it is narrated in one Prophetic Hadith: \"O Allah, all good is in Your Hands, and evil does not pertain to You.\" Al-Alusi: 11/124.\nThis verse and the Prophetic Hadith guide us to the proper way of speaking about Allah. Explain.\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِي يُسَيِّرُكُمۡ فِي ٱلۡبَرِّ وَٱلۡبَحۡرِۖ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا كُنتُمۡ فِي ٱلۡفُلۡكِ وَجَرَيۡنَ بِهِم بِرِيحٖ طَيِّبَةٖ وَفَرِحُواْ بِهَا جَآءَتۡهَا رِيحٌ عَاصِفٞ وَجَآءَهُمُ ٱلۡمَوۡجُ مِن كُلِّ مَكَانٖ وَظَنُّوٓاْ أَنَّهُمۡ أُحِيطَ بِهِمۡ دَعَوُاْ ٱللَّهَ مُخۡلِصِينَ لَهُ ٱلدِّينَ لَئِنۡ أَنجَيۡتَنَا مِنۡ هَٰذِهِۦ لَنَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلشَّٰكِرِينَ ٢٢\nThis verse indicates that when polytheists face distress, they do not supplicate other than Allah. At present times, you may see some people when faced with a grave danger in land or sea, they supplicate that which can neither benefit nor harm them, and neither see nor hear them, such as Al-Khidhr, Elias, or some Imam. But you never see any of them supplicate and humble himself solely to Allah, for it never crosses his mind that if he only supplicate Allah, he would survive all of these terrors. Al-Alusi: 11/130.\nThe current polytheists are sharply rebuked by this verse. Explain.\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِي يُسَيِّرُكُمۡ فِي ٱلۡبَرِّ وَٱلۡبَحۡرِۖ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا كُنتُمۡ فِي ٱلۡفُلۡكِ وَجَرَيۡنَ بِهِم بِرِيحٖ طَيِّبَةٖ وَفَرِحُواْ بِهَا جَآءَتۡهَا رِيحٌ عَاصِفٞ وَجَآءَهُمُ ٱلۡمَوۡجُ مِن كُلِّ مَكَانٖ وَظَنُّوٓاْ أَنَّهُمۡ أُحِيطَ بِهِمۡ دَعَوُاْ ٱللَّهَ مُخۡلِصِينَ لَهُ ٱلدِّينَ لَئِنۡ أَنجَيۡتَنَا مِنۡ هَٰذِهِۦ لَنَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلشَّٰكِرِينَ ٢٢\nAllah answers the supplication of the desperate one, even if he is a disbeliever because of absence of all means, and his sincere reversion to the Lord of all lords. Al-Qurtubi: 10/475.\nDoes Allah answer the supplication of the desperate disbeliever? Why?\nإِنَّمَا مَثَلُ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا كَمَآءٍ أَنزَلۡنَٰهُ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ فَٱخۡتَلَطَ بِهِۦ نَبَاتُ ٱلۡأَرۡضِ مِمَّا يَأۡكُلُ ٱلنَّاسُ وَٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمُ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَآ أَخَذَتِ ٱلۡأَرۡضُ زُخۡرُفَهَا وَٱزَّيَّنَتۡ وَظَنَّ أَهۡلُهَآ أَنَّهُمۡ قَٰدِرُونَ عَلَيۡهَآ أَتَىٰهَآ أَمۡرُنَا لَيۡلًا أَوۡ نَهَارٗا فَجَعَلۡنَٰهَا حَصِيدٗا كَأَن لَّمۡ تَغۡنَ بِٱلۡأَمۡسِۚ\nThe example of the quick termination of this life and its pleasures resembles the earth's plants when they become dry and turn into debris after they were thriving green adding beauty, colors and splendor to earth. Al-Biqai: 3/433.\nWhat is the similarity between the stages of this life's pleasures and that of the beauty of earth's plants?\nأَتَىٰهَآ أَمۡرُنَا لَيۡلًا أَوۡ نَهَارٗا فَجَعَلۡنَٰهَا حَصِيدٗا كَأَن لَّمۡ تَغۡنَ بِٱلۡأَمۡسِۚ\n(As if it had not flourished), Qatadah said: \"as if it was never blessed.\" Such are things after they perish, they are as if they had never existed. Similarly, the Prophet's Hadith: \"A person who led the most prosperous life in this world will be brought up and dipped once in the Hellfire. He will then be asked: 'Have you ever found any good or comfort?' He will reply: 'No.' And a person who had experienced extreme adversity in this world will be brought up and dipped once in the bliss (of Paradise). Then he will be asked: 'Did you ever face any hardship or misery?' He will reply: 'No.' \" Ibn Kathir: 2/395.\nThis verse makes all sins and pleasures of worldly life undesirable. Explain.\nكَذَٰلِكَ نُفَصِّلُ ٱلۡأٓيَٰتِ لِقَوۡمٖ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ ٢٤\n(As for the one who is heedless and turns away, the verses do not benefit him and the explanation does not dispel his doubts. Al-Saadi: 362.\nWhen does one benefit from the examples in the Quran?\nوَٱللَّهُ يَدۡعُوٓاْ إِلَىٰ دَارِ ٱلسَّلَٰمِ\nWhen Allah mentions the life of this world and its swift termination, He invites people to Paradise and encourages them to seek it. He calls it the Home of Peace. It is the Home of Peace because it is free from defects and miseries. Ibn Kathir: 2/395.\nWhy is Paradise called (Home of Peace)?\nwords\nالفُلكِThe ships\nعَاصِفٌA stormy wind\nيَبغُونَThey commit injustice\nزُخرُفَهَاEarth's splendor and fairest appearance\nحَصِيدًاField stubbles\nلَم تَغنَ بِالأَمسِIt had not flourished the day before\nدَارِ السَّلاَمِParadise"],[212,"§Yunus\ndeeds\nDo your utmost today to avoid looking at a forbidden thing, and prostrate much so that you may gaze upon the noble Countenance of Allah on the Day of Resurrection.\nDo good to a Muslim, today, to keep him from asking others with humility, so that Allah may recompense you with the best and more on the Day of Resurrection.\nThink of how difficult it is to run the affairs of your house, then reflect on how Allah runs the affairs of the whole universe without a single matter keeps Him distracted from another.\nguid\nBeware of defiant disobedience, for it has many levels, and the worst of them causes one to die as a disbeliever. May Allah saves us all.\nThe effects of sin on its perpetrator are numerous.\nIn this life, you may be able to talk yourself out of a predicament with a lie, but in the Hereafter you cannot.\nrefl\nلِّلَّذِينَ أَحۡسَنُواْ ٱلۡحُسۡنَىٰ وَزِيَادَةٞۖ وَلَا يَرۡهَقُ وُجُوهَهُمۡ قَتَرٞ وَلَا ذِلَّةٌۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ أَصۡحَٰبُ ٱلۡجَنَّةِۖ هُمۡ فِيهَا خَٰلِدُونَ ٢٦\nAs Allah calls His servants to the Home of Peace, it is as if people's hearts long for it and want to find out the deeds that will lead to it, so He tells us about them: (For those who have done good is the best [reward] - and more). Al-Saadi: 362.\nWhat is the link between this verse and the one before?\nلِّلَّذِينَ أَحۡسَنُواْ ٱلۡحُسۡنَىٰ وَزِيَادَةٞۖ\nMeaning: Those who do good in worshiping the Creator, in the sense that they worship Him knowing that He is watching them, and showing utter sincerity in their servitude to Him. So, they do all that they can of worship acts, and show as much kindness in words and deed to His servants as they can. Those are the ones who do good, and for them there will be (the best reward), namely Paradise, which is perfect in its beauty (and more), which is gazing upon the noble Countenance of Allah, hearing His words, attaining His pleasure, and having the joy of being close to Him. Thus, they will have attained all that one could wish or ask for. Al-Saadi: 362.\nHow does a Muslim become among those who do good?\nوَلَا يَرۡهَقُ وُجُوهَهُمۡ قَتَرٞ وَلَا ذِلَّةٌۚ\nMeaning: No harm will befall them in any way, because when harm befalls a person, that can be seen on his face, which changes and becomes gloomy. Al-Saadi: 362.\nAllah singles out the face as being protected in Paradise from distress? Why?\nوَقَالَ شُرَكَآؤُهُم مَّا كُنتُمۡ إِيَّانَا تَعۡبُدُونَ ٢٨\nThis is a sharp rebuke to the polytheists who worshiped, beside Him, others which can neither see nor hear, nor avail them in anything. In fact, this partner did not ask to be worshiped, nor did he accept it. He will disown them when they need him most. Ibn Kathir: 2/397.\nDescribe the shock in which the idols and graves worshipers will be on the Day of Resurrection when it will be judged between them and their gods.\nفَكَفَىٰ بِٱللَّهِ شَهِيدَۢا بَيۡنَنَا وَبَيۡنَكُمۡ إِن كُنَّا عَنۡ عِبَادَتِكُمۡ لَغَٰفِلِينَ ٢٩\n(And sufficient is Allah as a witness between us and you), He testifies to the fact that you did not single out us or Him for worship, rather you were wavering in between. This all indicate that mixed worshiping is in vain, and it is not even accepted by an inanimate object, if it could speak. Whoever is worthy of worship, is also worthy of sincerity to Him alone without partners, and no one is worthy of all that except the One Who is able to relieve the distress. Al-Biqai: 3/437.\nWho is only One worthy of worship? Why?\nإِن كُنَّا عَنۡ عِبَادَتِكُمۡ لَغَٰفِلِينَ ٢٩\nUnaware), because we have no souls, and hence we were not in a position to command worship nor accept it, so, the blame is on you not us. Al-Biqai: 3/437\nWhy cannot the worshiped objects censure their worshipers in this life?\nفَذَٰلِكُمُ ٱللَّهُ رَبُّكُمُ ٱلۡحَقُّۖ فَمَاذَا بَعۡدَ ٱلۡحَقِّ إِلَّا ٱلضَّلَٰلُۖ فَأَنَّىٰ تُصۡرَفُونَ ٣٢\nThis verse proves that there is no third status between truth and falsehood when it comes to religious beliefs. Truth can only exist on one side, which is in contrast to incidental issues. Ibn Juzay: 1/380.\nUsing this verse, how do you respond to one who dilutes the religious belief, claiming that each sect has some truth?\nwords\nيَرهَقُIt covers\nقَتَرٌDust, darkness\nعَاصِمٍA protector from Allah’s punishment\nفَزَيَّلنَاWe separate them\nتَبلُوIt examines, reviews"],[213,"§Yunus\ndeeds\nIdentify a piece of news that you heard or read today, then examine its authenticity based on validation and certainty to know the truth, and let that be your approach.\nIdentify an issue within the religious belief, with which you are not familiar, and inquire about it, as certain knowledge is required when it comes to religious beliefs, not assumptions .\nIdentify an individual or a group of people who speak ill of you, and pursue the reward from Allah by abandoning their companionship.\nguid\nOne must verify matters, and never rush to accept nor reject anything before he can ascertain its authenticity.\nTrue guidance is detailed in the Quran and is completed in Sunnah, and so there is no reference for true guidance except the Quran and Sunnah.\nRead the verses that challenge the polytheists, and think of their helplessness.\nrefl\nوَمَا يَتَّبِعُ أَكۡثَرُهُمۡ إِلَّا ظَنًّاۚ إِنَّ ٱلظَّنَّ لَا يُغۡنِي مِنَ ٱلۡحَقِّ شَيۡـًٔاۚ\n(And most of them follow nothing but assumptions), their chiefs who follow their assumption and speculation that these idols were their gods, and that they can intercede, but this was without proof. As for their followers, they follow them by imitation. Al-Qurtubi: 10/502.\nWhat causes the misguidance of the chiefs of religious innovation? What causes the misguidance of their followers?\nوَمَا يَتَّبِعُ أَكۡثَرُهُمۡ إِلَّا ظَنًّاۚ إِنَّ ٱلظَّنَّ لَا يُغۡنِي مِنَ ٱلۡحَقِّ شَيۡـًٔاۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَلِيمُۢ بِمَا يَفۡعَلُونَ ٣٦\n(And most of them follow nothing but assumptions) without verification, since it is not backed by evidence. (Indeed, assumptions are of no avail against the truth), this applies to religious beliefs for which certainty is required, in contrast to incidental matters. Ibn Juzay: 1/381.\nDo assumptions and imitation suffice for religious beliefs? What is required in such matters?\nوَتَفۡصِيلَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ لَا رَيۡبَ فِيهِ مِن رَّبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٣٧\nHe Is Allah Who takes care of all of His creation by His grace. One of the most significant ways in which He takes care of them is that He has revealed to them this Book which speaks of their religious and worldly interests and contains all noble characteristics and good deeds. Al-Saadi: 364.\nWhat is the link between the talk about explanation of the Book and concluding the verse with the attribute of Lordship?\nبَلۡ كَذَّبُواْ بِمَا لَمۡ يُحِيطُواْ بِعِلۡمِهِۦ وَلَمَّا يَأۡتِهِمۡ تَأۡوِيلُهُۥۚ كَذَٰلِكَ كَذَّبَ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِهِمۡۖ فَٱنظُرۡ كَيۡفَ كَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٣٩\nThis comparison illustrates few points, first: Their denial is a habit of stubborn disbelievers, so the polytheists would know that they were similar to past generations who denied the Messengers and learn a lesson. Second: This conveys a warning to them that they may be punished, similar to previous generations that people heard about and saw their destroyed homes. Third: A consolation to the Prophet (ﷺ) that he did not suffers from his people except similar to what previous Messengers had suffered from their people. Ibn Ashur: 11/173.\nThe attitudes of stubborn disbelievers are similar across history. Explain in light of this verse.\nبَلۡ كَذَّبُواْ بِمَا لَمۡ يُحِيطُواْ بِعِلۡمِهِۦ وَلَمَّا يَأۡتِهِمۡ تَأۡوِيلُهُۥۚ كَذَٰلِكَ كَذَّبَ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِهِمۡۖ فَٱنظُرۡ كَيۡفَ كَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٣٩\nThis indicates that one should verify all matters, and not hasten to accept or reject anything before one fully understands it. Al-Saadi: 365.\nHow does one deal with the news?\nوَمِنۡهُم مَّن يَسۡتَمِعُونَ إِلَيۡكَۚ أَفَأَنتَ تُسۡمِعُ ٱلصُّمَّ وَلَوۡ كَانُواْ لَا يَعۡقِلُونَ ٤٢\nThey listened to the Prophet (ﷺ) when he recited the revelation, not by way of seeking guidance but by way of passing the time, disbelieving and seeking out faults. This kind of listening is not beneficial and will not lead to attaining anything good. Al-Saadi: 365.\nWhy did not the polytheists benefit from listening to the Quran?\nوَمِنۡهُم مَّن يَسۡتَمِعُونَ إِلَيۡكَۚ أَفَأَنتَ تُسۡمِعُ ٱلصُّمَّ وَلَوۡ كَانُواْ لَا يَعۡقِلُونَ ٤٢\nAllah deems them as deaf because of the seal on their hearts, which means that you (the Prophet) cannot guide whom Allah deems deaf to listen to guidance. Al-Qurtubi: 10/507.\nWhy does Allah deem them as deaf despite having ears with which they can hear?\nwords\nفَأَنَّى تُؤفَكُونَSo, how are you deluded?\nلاَ يَهِدِّيHe who has no guidance\nيَأتِهِم تَأوِيلُهُIts warning has not yet been fulfilled against them"],[214,"§Yunus\ndeeds\nShare a message or give a talk in which you remind your brethren of how short the life of this world is.\nRead a reliable reference on the traits of the Prophet (ﷺ) - what he can and cannot do.\nSay, \"O Allah, I seek protection in Your pleasure from Your anger, and I seek protection in Your forgiveness from Your punishment.\"\nguid\nLife is but an hour, live it in obedience.\nIf you ever become wronged by others, just remember that on the Day of Resurrection, Allah will judge in justice, so be reassured.\nIf the Messenger (ﷺ) cannot benefit nor harm himself, so how would it be for those who are below him?\nrefl\nوَمِنۡهُم مَّن يَسۡتَمِعُونَ إِلَيۡكَۚ أَفَأَنتَ تُسۡمِعُ ٱلصُّمَّ وَلَوۡ كَانُواْ لَا يَعۡقِلُونَ ٤٢ وَمِنۡهُم مَّن يَنظُرُ إِلَيۡكَۚ أَفَأَنتَ تَهۡدِي ٱلۡعُمۡيَ وَلَوۡ كَانُواْ لَا يُبۡصِرُونَ ٤٣\nIf their minds, hearing and vision, which are the means of acquiring knowledge and learning facts, are not functioning, then what way do they have for reaching the truth? Al-Saadi: 365.\nWhat are the means for learning? How does one make the most of them to learn Sharia?\nوَمِنۡهُم مَّن يَنظُرُ إِلَيۡكَۚ\nThe words (And among them are some who look at you) indicate that looking at the Prophet (ﷺ) and his teachings, character, deeds and Message is the greatest evidence of his truthfulness and the soundness of what he brought; that is sufficient for one who has eyesight, and needs no further proof. Al-Saadi: 365.\nWhat is the importance of studying and teaching biography of the Prophet (ﷺ)?\nوَمِنۡهُم مَّن يَنظُرُ إِلَيۡكَۚ أَفَأَنتَ تَهۡدِي ٱلۡعُمۡيَ وَلَوۡ كَانُواْ لَا يُبۡصِرُونَ ٤٣\nThey look at you and see what Allah has given you in terms of discretion, noble personality and great conduct. There is in all of this clear evidence of your Prophethood for those who have reason and insight. They look, just like others do, but they do not receive guidance like them. Believers look at you with respect and dignity while disbelievers look at you with disdain. Ibn Kathir: 2/400.\nMuslims benefited from looking at the state of the Prophet (ﷺ) and his guidance, but polytheists did not. Why?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَظۡلِمُ ٱلنَّاسَ شَيۡـٔٗا وَلَٰكِنَّ ٱلنَّاسَ أَنفُسَهُمۡ يَظۡلِمُونَ ٤٤\nPeople wrong themselves by disbelieving, committing sins, and disobeying the command of their Creator. Al-Qurtubi: 10/507.\nHow does one wrong himself?\nوَيَوۡمَ يَحۡشُرُهُمۡ كَأَن لَّمۡ يَلۡبَثُوٓاْ إِلَّا سَاعَةٗ مِّنَ ٱلنَّهَارِ يَتَعَارَفُونَ بَيۡنَهُمۡۚ\nThese all are evidence of the brevity of the worldly life compared to the Hereafter. Ibn Kathir: 2/401.\nIn light of this verse, how do you view this worldly life?\nقُل لَّآ أَمۡلِكُ لِنَفۡسِي ضَرّٗا وَلَا نَفۡعًا إِلَّا مَا شَآءَ ٱللَّهُۗ\n(Say, \"I have no power to harm or benefit myself\"): I cannot provide myself with anything nor ward off any harm to it, (Except by the Will of Allah) then I can. Al-Baghawi: 2/365\nIf the Messenger (ﷺ) cannot benefit nor harm himself, can he do that for others?\nقُلۡ أَرَءَيۡتُمۡ إِنۡ أَتَىٰكُمۡ عَذَابُهُۥ بَيَٰتًا أَوۡ نَهَارٗا مَّاذَا يَسۡتَعۡجِلُ مِنۡهُ ٱلۡمُجۡرِمُونَ ٥٠\nThe word (bedtime) is used rather than \"night\", despite their similarity, to indicate sleep and heedlessness, and the fact that it is the time when the enemy is planning and seizing the opportunity of slackness, while the word \"night\" does not have this meaning. Al-Qasimi: 4/256.\nThe word (bedtime) is used rather than \"night.\" Why?\nwords\nيَنظُرُ إِلَيكَThey look at you\nأَرَأَيتُمTell me\nبَيَاتًاAt bedtime\nأَثُمَّIs it after\nوَيَستَنبِئُونَكَThey ask you"],[215,"§Yunus\ndeeds\nRansome yourself today from Allah's punishment, even with a little money, food or drink for charity, with a single Rak'a or a prostration before you wish to offer the world.\nRead this book: \"Kashf Al-Shubuhat\"; which refutes doubts using verses of the Quran.\nRead the Quran to cure your chest from worry and grief, and to remove doubts that shroud the hearts.\nguid\nIf one does not regret his sins and shortcomings today, he will definitely feel a greater regret on the Day of Resurrection.\nIf you wish to measure your love for Allah, think about this: Which do like more: The gains of the life of this world, or doing acts of obedience?\nNever say things that which you do not know about Allah, for it is a manifest way of loss.\nrefl\nأَلَآ إِنَّ لِلَّهِ مَا فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۗ أَلَآ إِنَّ وَعۡدَ ٱللَّهِ حَقّٞ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَهُمۡ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٥٥\nThe verse states that most of them do not know, which indicates that some of them know [the truth] but deny it out of arrogance. Ibn Ashur: 11/200.\nThe verse states that most of them do not know, but not all. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ قَدۡ جَآءَتۡكُم مَّوۡعِظَةٞ مِّن رَّبِّكُمۡ وَشِفَآءٞ لِّمَا فِي ٱلصُّدُورِ وَهُدٗى وَرَحۡمَةٞ لِّلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٥٧\n(A cure for [sickness] of the hearts), that is a cure for ignorance and doubts. Ibn Juzay: 1/382.\nWhy is the Quran a cure for the sickness of the hearts?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ قَدۡ جَآءَتۡكُم مَّوۡعِظَةٞ مِّن رَّبِّكُمۡ وَشِفَآءٞ لِّمَا فِي ٱلصُّدُورِ وَهُدٗى وَرَحۡمَةٞ لِّلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٥٧\nAllah describes the Quran with four attributes, which are the foundations of its perfection and features: An exhortation, a cure for [sickness] of the hearts, a guidance, and mercy. Ibn Ashur: 11/201.\nThe Quran is described with four attributes, which are the foundations of its perfection. What are they?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ قَدۡ جَآءَتۡكُم مَّوۡعِظَةٞ مِّن رَّبِّكُمۡ وَشِفَآءٞ لِّمَا فِي ٱلصُّدُورِ وَهُدٗى وَرَحۡمَةٞ لِّلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٥٧\n(A cure for [sickness] of the hearts), a cure for doubts, hypocrisy, differences and disputes. (A guidance) a guide for its followers. (And mercy) a blessing. (For the believers), they are singled out because they benefit from faith. Al-Qurtubi: 11/10.\nDoes every one benefit from the exhortation of the Quran and its cure?\nقُلۡ بِفَضۡلِ ٱللَّهِ وَبِرَحۡمَتِهِۦ فَبِذَٰلِكَ فَلۡيَفۡرَحُواْ\nAllah enjoins us to rejoice in His grace and mercy, because that is something that will result in feeling at ease, energized and grateful to Allah, and feeling a sense of power and eagerness to pursue knowledge and faith, which will motivate one to seek more of them. Al-Saadi: 367.\nAllah enjoins us to rejoice in His grace and mercy. Why?\nوَمَا ظَنُّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَفۡتَرُونَ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡكَذِبَ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَذُو فَضۡلٍ عَلَى ٱلنَّاسِ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَهُمۡ لَا يَشۡكُرُونَ ٦٠\n(Yet most of them are ungrateful), either they do not show gratitude for the blessings or they use them for sinful purposes, or they regard some of them as prohibited, and they reject what Allah has bestowed of His favors upon His servants. Al-Saadi: 367.\nWhat are the ways of being ungrateful to the favors of Allah?\nوَمَا تَكُونُ فِي شَأۡنٖ وَمَا تَتۡلُواْ مِنۡهُ مِن قُرۡءَانٖ وَلَا تَعۡمَلُونَ مِنۡ عَمَلٍ إِلَّا كُنَّا عَلَيۡكُمۡ شُهُودًا إِذۡ تُفِيضُونَ فِيهِۚ وَمَا يَعۡزُبُ عَن رَّبِّكَ مِن مِّثۡقَالِ ذَرَّةٖ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَلَا فِي ٱلسَّمَآءِ وَلَآ أَصۡغَرَ مِن ذَٰلِكَ وَلَآ أَكۡبَرَ إِلَّا فِي كِتَٰبٖ مُّبِينٍ ٦١\nHere Allah states that He is watching and seeing all that people do, when they are moving, and when they are resting. This is an implicit call to remember that He is always watching. Therefore,, remember that Allah is watching all your deeds, hence do them with sincerity while striving hard. Beware of doing what Allah dislikes, for He is watching you, and He knows what you disclose and what you conceal. Al-Saadi: 367-368.\nAllah states that his knowledge encompasses everything. Why?\nwords\nبِالقِسطِIn justice\nتَفتَرُونَYou fabricate lies\nشَأنٍA matter\nتُفِيضُونَYou are engaged in it\nيَعزُبُHides"],[216,"§Yunus\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, guide me with those whom You have guided, and be an ally to me along with those whom You are an ally to.\"\nIdentify some issues in which your whims contradict Sharia rules, then make a firm decision to put Sharia rules ahead of your whims, so that you will be an ally of Allah.\nRe-organize your daily activities, today, by going to sleep at the beginning of the night, and start your work at the beginning of the day in order to be in harmony with the natural order of things with which Allah is pleased.\nguid\nWhenever Sharia rules contradict your desire, hasten to put Sharia rules ahead, for this is the fear of Allah that will enable you to be an ally of Him.\nAllies of Allah are those who believe in Allah and fear Him, as it is stated by this verse. This will exclude polytheists, religious innovators and the defiantly disobedient.\nIf you hear hurtful, abusive and ill speech, do not grieve nor care because Allah, the Almighty, will honor His religion and His servants.\nrefl\nأَلَآ إِنَّ أَوۡلِيَآءَ ٱللَّهِ لَا خَوۡفٌ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وَلَا هُمۡ يَحۡزَنُونَ ٦٢\nThey grieve over adversities in this life, such as when the Prophet (ﷺ lost his son, he said: \"indeed, we are grieved over being separated from you, o Ibrahim.\" But, this is an affectional grief that abates with patience. The grief that does not afflict the believers is the permanent one, which is the humiliating grief over a defeat by their enemy, and the loss of their religion and state. Ibn Ashur: 11/218.\nWhat is the grief that does not afflict the believers? Does this contradict their griefs over adversities in this life?\nٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَكَانُواْ يَتَّقُونَ ٦٣\n(And fear Allah), using the present tense form indicates that they are consistently and repeatedly fear Allah. Ibn Ashur: 11/218.\nThis verse indicates that the believers consistently fear Allah. How?\nلَهُمُ ٱلۡبُشۡرَىٰ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَفِي ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِۚ\nGlad tidings for a believer in this world mean being spoken well of, praised, and loved by the believers. It also includes seeing good dreams and perceiving the kindness of Allah in enabling him to do the best of deeds and acquire the best of qualities, and by diverting from him bad characteristics. In the Hereafter, the first glad tidings the believers receive are at the time when their souls are taken in death. After that, in the grave, they receive the glad tidings of the good pleasure of Allah and eternal bliss. Then, in the Hereafter, they will receive the ultimate glad tidings of entering the gardens of bliss and salvation from the painful punishment. Al-Saadi: 368.\nState examples of the glad tidings for the believer in this life and the Hereafter.\nلَا تَبۡدِيلَ لِكَلِمَٰتِ ٱللَّهِۚ\nBecause He is the Truthful in all that He says and no one can go against what He wills and decrees. Al-Saadi: 368.\nWhat makes you confident that there is no change in Allah’s words?\nوَلَا يَحۡزُنكَ قَوۡلُهُمۡۘ إِنَّ ٱلۡعِزَّةَ لِلَّهِ جَمِيعًاۚ هُوَ ٱلسَّمِيعُ ٱلۡعَلِيمُ ٦٥\n(The verse, (Indeed, all power belongs to Allah) is a reason to ward off the grief of the Prophet (ﷺ), and that is why it is separated from the command at the beginning. It is as if the Prophet (r) would say: How cannot I grieve when the polytheists assail and threaten us while they have power and capability? Allah responds to him by confirming that their power is as good as non-existent because it is limited and temporary, but the true power and honor belong to Allah Who sent you to them. Ibn Ashur: 11/221.\nExplain the great difference between the power of Allah and that of polytheists.\nقَالُواْ ٱتَّخَذَ ٱللَّهُ وَلَدٗاۗ سُبۡحَٰنَهُۥۖ هُوَ ٱلۡغَنِيُّۖ لَهُۥ مَا فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ إِنۡ عِندَكُم مِّن سُلۡطَٰنِۢ بِهَٰذَآۚ أَتَقُولُونَ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ مَا لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٦٨\nThis verse affirms that every claim without proof is mere ignorance, that religious beliefs necessitate conclusive evidence, and imitation does not lead to the right guidance. Al-Alusi: 11/207.\nWhat is the risk in neglecting the authentic proof and knowledge of Sharia?\nقُلۡ إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَفۡتَرُونَ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡكَذِبَ لَا يُفۡلِحُونَ ٦٩\nMeaning: They will not be saved; it is also said that they will not last for long in this life. Al-Baghawi: 2/371.\nWhat is the punishment of those who fabricate lies against Allah?\nwords\nسُبحَانَهُExalted is He, Glory be to Him\nسُلطَانٍA proof, evidence"],[217,"§Yunus\ndeeds\nAfter reading the story of Noah (u), tell it to some of your relatives and friends because Allah says to His Prophet (ﷺ)\nLend a helping hand to one who calls others to Allah, or to a charitable organization, in pursuit of Allah's reward.\nSeek refuge with Allah from a seal on your heart, for one with a sealed heart can never carry out any good.\nguid\nA believer can be saved from the harm of people only by the grace of Allah, so seek refuge only with Him.\nNever reject the truth, for its rejection may cause a seal on your heart, and you will not be able to find a way for repentance afterward.\nFalse accusations is a method used in the past and present by the people of falsehood, transgression, and corruption.\nrefl\nثُمَّ لَا يَكُنۡ أَمۡرُكُمۡ عَلَيۡكُمۡ غُمَّةٗ ثُمَّ ٱقۡضُوٓاْ إِلَيَّ وَلَا تُنظِرُونِ ٧١\n(Then carry it out upon me), do what you want against me. In essence, Noah (u) said to his people: If calling you to Allah has become unbearable, then carry out your plans against me, for I do not care since I rely on Allah and entrust all my affairs to Him. Ibn Juzay: 1/385.\nDisplaying strength at times of hardships comes from a deed of the heart? What is it?\nفَإِن تَوَلَّيۡتُمۡ فَمَا سَأَلۡتُكُم مِّنۡ أَجۡرٍۖ إِنۡ أَجۡرِيَ إِلَّا عَلَى ٱللَّهِۖ\n(Then I have not asked you) for conveying the message (for any reward) a gain or compensation; (my reward), my recompense (is only with Allah). Al-Baghawi: 2/372.\nThe verse states a sign of truth by which you can distinguish between Al-Sunnah scholars and Al-Bid'a (religious innovation) scholars. What is it?\nفَكَذَّبُوهُ فَنَجَّيۡنَٰهُ وَمَن مَّعَهُۥ فِي ٱلۡفُلۡكِ وَجَعَلۡنَٰهُمۡ خَلَٰٓئِفَ وَأَغۡرَقۡنَا ٱلَّذِينَ كَذَّبُواْ بَِٔايَٰتِنَاۖ فَٱنظُرۡ كَيۡفَ كَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلۡمُنذَرِينَ ٧٣\nThe verse mentions the saving of Noah (u) before mentioning the drowning -from which the saving occurred- to indicate that his saving is more important to Allah than drowning those who rejected him, and to hasten in giving the good news to Muslims who listen to this narrative. Ibn Ashur: 11/243.\nWhat is the benefit of mentioning the saving of Noah (u) before that of drowning his people?\nثُمَّ بَعَثۡنَا مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِۦ رُسُلًا إِلَىٰ قَوۡمِهِمۡ فَجَآءُوهُم بِٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتِ فَمَا كَانُواْ لِيُؤۡمِنُواْ بِمَا كَذَّبُواْ بِهِۦ مِن قَبۡلُۚ كَذَٰلِكَ نَطۡبَعُ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِ ٱلۡمُعۡتَدِينَ ٧٤\n(We seal the hearts of the transgressors), those who exceed the usual limits of disbelief and stubbornness. We, therefore, keep them from accepting the truth and following the right guidance. Al-Alusi: 11/216.\nIn light of this verse, what are the obstacles to the right guidance?\nثُمَّ بَعَثۡنَا مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِم مُّوسَىٰ وَهَٰرُونَ إِلَىٰ فِرۡعَوۡنَ وَمَلَإِيْهِۦ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا فَٱسۡتَكۡبَرُواْ وَكَانُواْ قَوۡمٗا مُّجۡرِمِينَ ٧٥\nAllah mentions the narrative of Moses (u) and Pharaoh often in His sacred Book (the Quran) because it is one of the most fascinating stories. Pharaoh was extremely wary of the coming of Moses, but the divine will made him to raise this boy, whom he is wary of, in his house as a son to him. When he grew up, he was caused to leave, then Allah bestowed Prophethood on him, and spoke to him with a message to Pharaoh calling him to Allah. Ibn Kathir: 2/408.\nThe narrative of Moses (u) and Pharaoh is mentioned often in the Quran. Why?\nقَالُوٓاْ أَجِئۡتَنَا لِتَلۡفِتَنَا عَمَّا وَجَدۡنَا عَلَيۡهِ ءَابَآءَنَا وَتَكُونَ لَكُمَا ٱلۡكِبۡرِيَآءُ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَمَا نَحۡنُ لَكُمَا بِمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٧٨\n(You two might become supreme), which is greatness, sovereignty and authority. Al-Qurtubi: 11/28.\nAccusing those who call others to Allah that they are after authority is an old routine. Explain in light of this verse.\nقَالُوٓاْ أَجِئۡتَنَا لِتَلۡفِتَنَا عَمَّا وَجَدۡنَا عَلَيۡهِ ءَابَآءَنَا وَتَكُونَ لَكُمَا ٱلۡكِبۡرِيَآءُ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَمَا نَحۡنُ لَكُمَا بِمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٧٨\nArguments cannot be warded off except by means of proof and evidence. If a person brings truth and his message is countered with such flimsy arguments, this indicates that the one who presents this argument is unable to refute what his opponent stated. If he had sound proofing and a sound argument, he would state it, and would not resort to saying, \"Your intention is..., your aim is ...\", regardless of whether his accusation is correct or not. Al-Saadi: 371.\nThe verse depicts a method used by the people of falsehood. Explain.\nwords\nكَبُرَIt has become burdensome\nفَأَجمِعُواResolve, and gather\nغُمَّةًObscure\nخَلاَئِفَSuccessors to the disbelievers\nوَمَلَإيهِThe chiefs of his people\nلِتَلفِتَنَاTo turn us away"],[218,"§Yunus\ndeeds\nShare a message in which you warn against magic and magicians.\nInvoke Allah against those who fight Islam and Muslims with this:\nRecite these blessed verses on yourself and one whom you believe is afflicted with evil eye or magic, for these verses have healing effect, if Allah wills.\nguid\nCorrupt deeds, even if they are powerful, will come to naught, while good deeds last and continue to benefit its doer and people.\nThe youth are more accepting of the truth, so do not neglect to invite them to Allah, no matter how playful or reckless they are.\nPutting your trust in Allah is a must in order to carry the burden of calling others to Allah and obeying Him.\nrefl\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَ ٱلسَّحَرَةُ قَالَ لَهُم مُّوسَىٰٓ أَلۡقُواْ مَآ أَنتُم مُّلۡقُونَ ٨٠\nMoses (u) directed them to throw their magic first in order to show his powerful evidence; for a competitor to precede in a contest on which frightening and camouflage is based will be more likely to influence the attendance and win their admiration. Ibn Ashur: 11/254.\nWhy did Moses (u) direct them to throw their magic first?\nفَلَمَّآ أَلۡقَوۡاْ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ مَا جِئۡتُم بِهِ ٱلسِّحۡرُۖ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ سَيُبۡطِلُهُۥٓ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يُصۡلِحُ عَمَلَ ٱلۡمُفۡسِدِينَ ٨١\nMagicians are corruptors because their intention is to mislead the minds of people and keep them subjugated to them, not knowing how things are done, so they become like a toy controlled by the magicians, and are unable to find a way to guide themselves to the truth. The magicians whom Moses (u) addressed, however, had done even greater corruption because they tried to refute the truth, the right religion, and spread shirk and misguidance. Ibn Ashur: 11/257.\nMagicians are of different degrees in their corruption. Explain.\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يُصۡلِحُ عَمَلَ ٱلۡمُفۡسِدِينَ ٨١\nThis applies to any mischief-maker who does and plans anything. His deeds will come to naught and fail. Even if what he does may meet with some measure of success at some time, ultimately it will diminish and be destroyed. As for those who do good, seeking thereby the Countenance of Allah and they do beneficial deeds that are enjoined, Allah will guide them, refine their deeds and cause them to grow and develop. Al-Saadi: 371.\nWhat is the end result of corrupt deeds? What is the end result of good deeds?\nفَمَآ ءَامَنَ لِمُوسَىٰٓ إِلَّا ذُرِّيَّةٞ مِّن قَوۡمِهِۦ\nThe youth are more accepting of the truth and are quicker to follow it, unlike their elders who grew up with disbelief. Because of what remains in their hearts of false beliefs, the elders are further from the truth than others. Al-Saadi: 371.\nWhat is the reason that most of those who believed in Moses were youth?\nفَقَالُواْ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ تَوَكَّلۡنَا رَبَّنَا لَا تَجۡعَلۡنَا فِتۡنَةٗ لِّلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٨٥\nMeaning: Do not enable them to torture us, so that they would say, \"If those were on the right path, we would not had been able to torture them.\" Hence, the disbelievers would become misguided. Ibn Juzay: 1/386.\nWhat was the aim of Moses (u) and his people with this supplication?\nفَقَالُواْ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ تَوَكَّلۡنَا رَبَّنَا لَا تَجۡعَلۡنَا فِتۡنَةٗ لِّلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٨٥ وَنَجِّنَا بِرَحۡمَتِكَ مِنَ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ٨٦\nEven though they were complying with the command of Moses (u), uttering the reliance upon Allah before invoking Him indicates that it is within the right of one who invokes Allah to base his request on the fact that he is putting his trust in Him, which makes his request more likely to be answered. One should not think that putting his trust in Allah contradicts invoking Him; rather, it is a means to what he wishes for. Al-Alusi: 11/226.\nDoes proper reliance upon Allah contradict supplicating Him?\nفَلَا يُؤۡمِنُواْ حَتَّىٰ يَرَوُاْ ٱلۡعَذَابَ ٱلۡأَلِيمَ ٨٨\nThis prayer was from Moses (u) because he was angry for the sake of Allah and His religion. He prayed against Pharaoh and his chiefs when he was certain that there was no good in them and nothing would come out of them. In the same way, Noah (u) prayed and said: (My Lord, leave not one of the disbelievers on the earth ` If You leave them, they will mislead Your servants, and they will beget none but wicked disbelievers.) [71:26-27]. Ibn Kathir: 2/411.\nWhy did Moses (u) invoke Allah against Pharaoh and his chiefs?\nwords\nوَيُحِقُّHe will establish\nتَبَوَّءَاYou make\nاطمِس عَلَى أَموَالِهِمDestroy their wealth\nوَاشدُد عَلَى قُلُوبِهِمHarden their hearts"],[219,"§Yunus\ndeeds\nInvoke Allah persistently for something that is important to you while having good expectations of Him.\nRemember a sin that you had committed, and hasten to repent before it is too late.\nGather questions for which you need answers, then contact one of the scholars and ask him about them.\nguid\nYour supplication may be answered after a while.\nBe sure to say: \"Amen\" whenever you hear a supplication, for saying \"Amen\" is in itself a supplication.\nHasten to repent, for the end time for repentance may startle you.\nrefl\nقَالَ قَدۡ أُجِيبَت دَّعۡوَتُكُمَا\nThis is addressed to both Moses (u) and Aaron (u), but the previous verse mentions that Moses (u) alone was supplicating which means that Aaron (u) was saying: \"Amen.\" Ibn Juzay: 1/387.\nThis verse proves that supplication is answered for the supplicant and the one who says: \"Amen.\" Explain.\nقَالَ قَدۡ أُجِيبَت دَّعۡوَتُكُمَا فَٱسۡتَقِيمَا وَلَا تَتَّبِعَآنِّ سَبِيلَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٨٩\nIn addition to answering their supplication, Allah enjoined them to be steadfast on the straight path, which is done in gratitude to Allah for His favor upon them. Answering His servant’s supplication is a favor from Allah that merits offering gratitude to Him. The greatest form of gratitude to Allah is obeying Him. The essence of steadfastness is uprightness, which is the opposite of deviance, and it often used to mean adhering to the truth and the right course. Ibn Ashur: 11/273.\nWhat is the meaning of \"steadfastness\"? Allah enjoined them to be steadfast after accepting their supplication, why?\nحَتَّىٰٓ إِذَآ أَدۡرَكَهُ ٱلۡغَرَقُ قَالَ ءَامَنتُ أَنَّهُۥ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا ٱلَّذِيٓ ءَامَنَتۡ بِهِۦ بَنُوٓاْ إِسۡرَٰٓءِيلَ وَأَنَا۠ مِنَ ٱلۡمُسۡلِمِينَ ٩٠\nBelief is not beneficial then, and repentance is accepted only before facing death, but after witnessing one's own death, no repentance will be accepted. Al-Qurtubi: 11/45.\nWhen does accepting repentance and faith end?\nحَتَّىٰٓ إِذَآ أَدۡرَكَهُ ٱلۡغَرَقُ قَالَ ءَامَنتُ أَنَّهُۥ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا ٱلَّذِيٓ ءَامَنَتۡ بِهِۦ بَنُوٓاْ إِسۡرَٰٓءِيلَ وَأَنَا۠ مِنَ ٱلۡمُسۡلِمِينَ ٩٠\nThis is the way of Allah; once the disbelievers reach the point at which they have no choice but to believe, belief will not benefit them because their belief is based on what they see with their own eyes, like the belief of one who is resurrected. The only belief or faith that is of benefit is the faith in the unseen. Al-Saadi: 372.\nAllah did not accept the belief of Pharaoh, why? What is the acceptable belief to Allah?\nوَإِنَّ كَثِيرٗا مِّنَ ٱلنَّاسِ عَنۡ ءَايَٰتِنَا لَغَٰفِلُونَ ٩٢\nHence, they may come across signs repeatedly, but they do not benefit from them because they have no interest in them. In contrast, the one who is alert and focused sees of the signs of Allah that which is the greatest evidence of the soundness of what the Messengers told us. Al-Saadi: 373.\nWhat prevents most people from benefiting from the abundant signs of Allah?\nفَمَا ٱخۡتَلَفُواْ حَتَّىٰ جَآءَهُمُ ٱلۡعِلۡمُۚ\nThis is the problem that the followers of the true religion are faced with: if satan fails to make them obey him by abandoning religion completely, he strives to stir up troubles among them and create enmity and resentment among them, so that differences arise between them that lead them to brand one another as misguided, and developing grudges against one another, which will delight Iblees. Otherwise, as their Lord is one, their Messenger is one, their religion is one, and their public interests are the same, why would they differ in such a way that divides them, weakens them, dissolves the bonds between them, and thus is detrimental to their religious and worldly interests, and this detracts from their religious commitment. Al-Saadi: 373.\nWhat is the problem that weakened Muslims despite them having the right knowledge?\nفَإِن كُنتَ فِي شَكّٖ مِّمَّآ أَنزَلۡنَآ إِلَيۡكَ فَسۡـَٔلِ ٱلَّذِينَ يَقۡرَءُونَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ مِن قَبۡلِكَۚ\nThis is a guidance to anyone who has doubts about religious issues to seek knowledge from scholars, and do that swiftly as indicated by the verse. Al-Alusi: 11/252.\nWhat is the cure for doubts that come to mind?\nwords\nفَاستَقِيمَاBe steadfast in the straight path\nوَلاَ تَتَّبِعَانِّDo not follow\nوَجَاوَزنَاWe took them across the sea\nبَغيًا وَعَدوًاIn tyranny and enmity\nنُنَجِّيكَWe throw your body out of the sea\nبَوَّأنَاWe settled them\nمُبَوَّأَ صِدقٍA blessed land in Levant and Egypt"],[220,"§Yunus\ndeeds\nSit in solitude and gaze up at the sky or the mountains and reflect on their beauty and signs.\nSay, \"O Allah I seek refuge in You lest I associate anything with You while I know it, and I seek Your forgiveness for what I do not know.\"\nWrite down this verse and send it to whoever invokes other than Allah.\nguid\nRepentance is accepted before punishment strikes and seeing the signs of the end.\nBear in mind that guidance and belief are in the Hands of Allah, the Almighty, and if He had Willed, He would have made all mankind believers.\nWhen Allah sends His punishment onto the oppressors and disbelievers, His promise stands firm for His allies by saving them from the punishment.\nrefl\nفَلَوۡلَا كَانَتۡ قَرۡيَةٌ ءَامَنَتۡ فَنَفَعَهَآ إِيمَٰنُهَآ\nMeaning: Not one of them benefitted from believing once they had seen the punishment. The wisdom behind it is obvious; believing under compulsion does not constitute real faith, and if the punishment which compelled them to believe was averted, they would go back to disbelief. Al-Saadi: 374.\nThe faith of one who has seen the punishment doe not benefit him. Why?\nفَلَوۡلَا كَانَتۡ قَرۡيَةٌ ءَامَنَتۡ فَنَفَعَهَآ إِيمَٰنُهَآ إِلَّا قَوۡمَ يُونُسَ لَمَّآ ءَامَنُواْ كَشَفۡنَا عَنۡهُمۡ عَذَابَ ٱلۡخِزۡيِ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَمَتَّعۡنَٰهُمۡ إِلَىٰ حِينٖ ٩٨\nPerhaps the reason for that is that if the others who were destroyed had been given a second chance, they would have gone back to that which they were forbidden to do. As for the people of Jonah (u), Allah knew that their faith would continue, and indeed they remained steadfast. Al-Saadi: 374.\nWhat is the reason that the people of Jonah (u) benefitted from faith after seeing the punishment?\nوَلَوۡ شَآءَ رَبُّكَ لَأٓمَنَ مَن فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ كُلُّهُمۡ جَمِيعًاۚ أَفَأَنتَ تُكۡرِهُ ٱلنَّاسَ حَتَّىٰ يَكُونُواْ مُؤۡمِنِينَ ٩٩\nThis is a consolation to the Prophet (ﷺ) since he was doing his utmost to have all people believed, but Allah tells him that no one can believe or go astray except by Allah's will. Al-Baghawi: 2/381.\nThe Prophet's (ﷺ) mercy for his Muslim nation has reached a very high level. Explain.\nفَهَلۡ يَنتَظِرُونَ إِلَّا مِثۡلَ أَيَّامِ ٱلَّذِينَ خَلَوۡاْ مِن قَبۡلِهِمۡۚ\nMeaning: Do these people who disbelieve in the signs of Allah expect anything after those signs have become clear (except for the same punishment that befell those who came before them), namely destruction and punishment, for they have done the same as those people did, and the laws of Allah are applicable to earlier and later generations alike. Al-Saadi: 374.\nThe way of Allah in dealing with disbelievers does not change. Explain in light of this verse.\nثُمَّ نُنَجِّي رُسُلَنَا وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْۚ كَذَٰلِكَ حَقًّا عَلَيۡنَا نُنجِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ١٠٣\nAllah took it upon Himself by virtue of His benevolence, favor and promise. No one can dictate what Allah can or cannot do; for that is only when one person deals with another. Ibn Taimyah: 3/501\nWhat is meant by Allah’s saying that He took it upon Himself?\nثُمَّ نُنَجِّي رُسُلَنَا وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْۚ كَذَٰلِكَ حَقًّا عَلَيۡنَا نُنجِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ١٠٣\nMeaning: It is Our way that when We punish some people, We save the Messengers and believers from among them. Al-Qurtubi: 11/58.\nDoes the punishment of annihilation reaches those who are guided?\nوَلَا تَدۡعُ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ مَا لَا يَنفَعُكَ وَلَا يَضُرُّكَۖ فَإِن فَعَلۡتَ فَإِنَّكَ إِذٗا مِّنَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ١٠٦\nThe aim of this command is to alert people to the grave nature of this action [invoking others besides Allah], even if it is done by the most honorable man, he would still be among the transgressors. Ibn Ashur: 11/305.\nIf the Prophet (ﷺ) would never invoke others besides Allah, then what is aim of addressing him with it?\nwords\nالرِّجسَThe punishment\nوَمَا تُغنِيOf no avail\nخَلَواThose who passed before you\nأَقِم وَجهَكَ لِلدِّينِBe steadfast on Islam and devoted to it\nحَنِيفًاInclining from shirk to the Oneness of Allah"],[221,"§Hud, Yunus\ndeeds\nSeek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him seventy times today.\nIdentify your biggest wishes or needs, and invoke Allah, the Almighty, persistently for them while having good expectations of Him.\nSeek refuge with Allah from envy. When Allah decrees favors for one of His servants, nothing can withhold His gift and generosity.\nguid\nBe patient when it comes to obeying Allah and evading sins, as whoever obeys Allah is subjected to hardships, especially in times of trials.\nKnow that Allah, the Almighty, is the best of judges; He Who decreed the victory of his loyal servants, the high raise of their repute, and the abasement of their enemy.\nOne of the signs of the Quran's inimitability is the fact that it is made up of these abbreviated letters, yet the Arabs were unable to produce a single Surah like it.\nrefl\nوَإِن يَمۡسَسۡكَ ٱللَّهُ بِضُرّٖ فَلَا كَاشِفَ لَهُۥٓ إِلَّا هُوَۖ وَإِن يُرِدۡكَ بِخَيۡرٖ فَلَا رَآدَّ لِفَضۡلِهِۦۚ يُصِيبُ بِهِۦ مَن يَشَآءُ مِنۡ عِبَادِهِۦۚ وَهُوَ ٱلۡغَفُورُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ١٠٧\nOnce a person understands, on the basis of definitive proof, that Allah is the only One Who grants good and removes hardship and distress, and that no one in creation has any control over these things unless Allah causes it to happen at his servant's hand, he will be certain that Allah is the Truth and that whatever they call upon besides Him is false. Al-Saadi: 375.\nIn light of this verse, explain how you will give advice to one who is attached to creatures and heedless of the Creator.\nوَٱتَّبِعۡ مَا يُوحَىٰٓ إِلَيۡكَ وَٱصۡبِرۡ حَتَّىٰ يَحۡكُمَ ٱللَّهُۚ وَهُوَ خَيۡرُ ٱلۡحَٰكِمِينَ ١٠٩\nAllah combines patience with good deeds, in general and in particular, and says, (And follow what is revealed to you, and be patient until Allah will judge. And He is the best of judges). In following what is revealed to him, he attains piety through believing His words and complying with His commands. Ibn Taimyah: 3/501.\nWhat is the true means for attaining piety?\nالٓرۚ كِتَٰبٌ أُحۡكِمَتۡ ءَايَٰتُهُۥ ثُمَّ فُصِّلَتۡ مِن لَّدُنۡ حَكِيمٍ خَبِيرٍ ١\nThis Surah, (Hud), consists of detailed narratives of past generations and how they were destroyed by Allah for their disbelief. When that is recited by people of sure faith, it becomes so real to them, and they feel in their hearts the might and the great power of Allah so much that if they were to die from the horror, it would be rightful for them. But Allah, Blessed and Exalted is His Name, is Merciful to them during these times so they can recite His words. Al-Qurtubi: 11/64.\nWhat is the topic of Surat Hud? What is its effect on faithful righteous people when they read it?\nمِن لَّدُنۡ حَكِيمٍ خَبِيرٍ ١\nAs its perfection and clarification come from Allah, the Most Wise, the All-Aware, then do not ask about how great and majestic it is and how it encompasses perfect wisdom and vast mercy. Al-Saadi: 376.\nWhat is the benefit of knowing that the Quran is revealed by the Most Wise, the All-Aware?\nوَأَنِ ٱسۡتَغۡفِرُواْ رَبَّكُمۡ ثُمَّ تُوبُوٓاْ إِلَيۡهِ يُمَتِّعۡكُم مَّتَٰعًا حَسَنًا إِلَىٰٓ أَجَلٖ مُّسَمّٗى وَيُؤۡتِ كُلَّ ذِي فَضۡلٖ فَضۡلَهُۥۖ وَإِن تَوَلَّوۡاْ فَإِنِّيٓ أَخَافُ عَلَيۡكُمۡ عَذَابَ يَوۡمٖ كَبِيرٍ ٣\nA righteous person said: \"Asking for Allah's forgiveness without ceasing the sin is the repentance of liars.\" It is said that asking for forgiveness is mentioned first because forgiveness is the desired objective, and repentance is a means to it. Moreover, the intended meaning may be as follows: Ask for His forgiveness from minor sins, and repent to Him from major ones. Al-Qurtubi: 11/67.\nAsking for forgiveness precedes repenting. Why?\nوَأَنِ ٱسۡتَغۡفِرُواْ رَبَّكُمۡ ثُمَّ تُوبُوٓاْ إِلَيۡهِ يُمَتِّعۡكُم مَّتَٰعًا حَسَنًا إِلَىٰٓ أَجَلٖ مُّسَمّٗى وَيُؤۡتِ كُلَّ ذِي فَضۡلٖ فَضۡلَهُۥۖ وَإِن تَوَلَّوۡاْ فَإِنِّيٓ أَخَافُ عَلَيۡكُمۡ عَذَابَ يَوۡمٖ كَبِيرٍ ٣\nMeaning: Allah will provide you with a good livelihood in peace and abundance. He will reward every doer of good deeds in this life and in the Hereafter. Al-Baghawi: 2/385-386.\nWhat are the results of asking for Allah's forgiveness (Istighfar)?\nأَلَآ إِنَّهُمۡ يَثۡنُونَ صُدُورَهُمۡ لِيَسۡتَخۡفُواْ مِنۡهُۚ أَلَا حِينَ يَسۡتَغۡشُونَ ثِيَابَهُمۡ يَعۡلَمُ مَا يُسِرُّونَ وَمَا يُعۡلِنُونَۚ إِنَّهُۥ عَلِيمُۢ بِذَاتِ ٱلصُّدُورِ ٥\nIt is said that when the Prophet (ﷺ) came across the disbelievers, they turned their backs to him, out of hatred, lest they see him. Ibn Juzay: 1/390.\nWhat is meant by turning away their breast? Why did they do that?\nwords\nفُصِّلَتEnjoining and forbidding are presented in detail in the verses of the Quran\nتُوبُوا إِلَيهِTurn to Him with regret\nيَثنُونَ صُدُورَهُمThey turn away their breasts\nلِيَستَخفُوا مِنهُTo conceal their feelings from Allah\nيَستَغشُونَThey cover themselves in their clothing"],[222,"§Hud\ndeeds\nReflect upon the tiny creatures, and how the Creator guarantees their provisions, then pursue a means for your provision while relying on Allah.\nIdentify a blessing that you had, then it was taken away, and thank Allah for His decree in both situations.\nReflect upon yourself; if you find that you are distressed for missing out on this life's adornment, then ask for Allah's forgiveness often.\nguid\nThere is no limit to the knowledge of Allah, and His sustaining of the life of all of His creation.\nDo not be deluded by the respite given by Allah to those who disobey Him.\nThe true value of a servant to His Lord is by his good deed, not his wealth.\nrefl\nوَمَا مِن دَآبَّةٖ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ إِلَّا عَلَى ٱللَّهِ رِزۡقُهَا وَيَعۡلَمُ مُسۡتَقَرَّهَا وَمُسۡتَوۡدَعَهَاۚ كُلّٞ فِي كِتَٰبٖ مُّبِينٖ ٦\nThis is a promise and an assurance from Allah. If one asks: how can something which is a favor from Him becomes (upon Allah)? The answer is that any promise made by Allah becomes a reality since He never breaks His promise. Ibn Juzay: 1/391.\nHow can something which is a favor from Allah becomes (upon Allah)?\nلِيَبۡلُوَكُمۡ أَيُّكُمۡ أَحۡسَنُ عَمَلٗاۗ\nAllah did not say, \"Which of you has done the most deeds.\" Rather, He says, (best in deeds). A deed cannot be considered a good deed until it is done sincerely for Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, and it must be in accordance with the Sunnah of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ). Whenever a deed lacks one of these conditions, then it is null and void. Ibn Kathir: 2/419.\nWhat is the difference between \"most deeds\", and (best in deeds)? Why is the latter term used?\nلِيَبۡلُوَكُمۡ أَيُّكُمۡ أَحۡسَنُ عَمَلٗاۗ\nThe best deed is attained by two things, first: It is done sincerely for Allah, seeking thereby the Countenance of Allah, and not associating partners with Him. Second: It is ordained by Allah, loved by Him, conformed to the rules of Sharia, and not invented. Fudhail bin Iyadh said about this verse (which of you is best in deed): \"The deed that is done sincerely and correctly.\" Ibn Taimyah: 3/507.\nHow does a deed become (best)?\nوَلَئِنۡ أَذَقۡنَا ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ مِنَّا رَحۡمَةٗ ثُمَّ نَزَعۡنَٰهَا مِنۡهُ إِنَّهُۥ لَيَـُٔوسٞ كَفُورٞ ٩ وَلَئِنۡ أَذَقۡنَٰهُ نَعۡمَآءَ بَعۡدَ ضَرَّآءَ مَسَّتۡهُ لَيَقُولَنَّ ذَهَبَ ٱلسَّيِّـَٔاتُ عَنِّيٓۚ إِنَّهُۥ لَفَرِحٞ فَخُورٌ ١٠\nMan is just as described by Allah; when he faces hardship after prosperity, he becomes despaired of having an end to the hardship in the future, and is ungrateful for the prosperity he had before. When he gains prosperity after hardship, he feels secure from ever facing hardship again in the future, and forgets what he has been through by saying: (\"All my ills are gone,\" and becomes exultant and boastful). Ibn Taimyah: 3/508.\nExplain the state of man when he is tried by prosperity and by hardship.\nإِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ صَبَرُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ لَهُم مَّغۡفِرَةٞ وَأَجۡرٞ كَبِيرٞ ١١\nOne of the indications of patience is expecting relief. The term (who are patient) is used instead of \"who believe\" to give the opposite meaning to the state of disbelievers mentioned in the previous verse, (he becomes utterly despaired and ungrateful). Ibn Ashur: 12/15.\nThe verse uses the term (who are patient) instead of \"who believe.\" Why?\nفَلَعَلَّكَ تَارِكُۢ بَعۡضَ مَا يُوحَىٰٓ إِلَيۡكَ وَضَآئِقُۢ بِهِۦ صَدۡرُكَ أَن يَقُولُواْ لَوۡلَآ أُنزِلَ عَلَيۡهِ كَنزٌ أَوۡ جَآءَ مَعَهُۥ مَلَكٌۚ\nThese verses indicate that it is inappropriate for someone who calls people to Allah to be deterred by the objections and criticisms of people; especially if this criticism is baseless and does not undermine the message to which he is calling them. Al-Saadi: 378.\nIn this verse, there is a lesson to those who call others to Allah. What is it?\nفَلَعَلَّكَ تَارِكُۢ بَعۡضَ مَا يُوحَىٰٓ إِلَيۡكَ وَضَآئِقُۢ بِهِۦ صَدۡرُكَ أَن يَقُولُواْ لَوۡلَآ أُنزِلَ عَلَيۡهِ كَنزٌ أَوۡ جَآءَ مَعَهُۥ مَلَكٌۚ\nThe breadth of mind of the Prophet (ﷺ) is indicated in this verse by the use of a variation of the adjective (distressed) in the original Arabic text. Ibn Juzay: 1/392.\nHow does this verse indicate the breadth of mind of the Prophet (ﷺ)?\nwords\nمُستَقَرَّهَاIts resting place in life and after death\nوَمُستَودَعَهَاThe place of its death\nأُمَّةٍ مَعدُودَةٍA determined time\nمَا يَحبِسُهُWhat is holding it back?\nوَحَاقَEncompassed them from all sides"],[223,"§Hud\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to grant you knowledge and understanding in Islam, and beware of consuming unlawful provision so that you stand on clear evidence from your Lord.\nStrive to invite a heedless or a disbeliever person today, and do not be distressed over his lack of response, for his guidance is at the Hand of Allah.\nWhen you leave your house, say, \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You lest I stray or be led astray, slip or made to slip, cause injustice or suffer injustice, or behave foolishly or be treated foolishly.\"\nguid\nDo a good deed to which the witnesses will testify for you on the Day of Judgment.\nBeware of conversing in the rules of Shariah without knowledge, for that would amount to fabricating lies against Allah.\nAvoid wrongdoing yourself by committing sins, or wrongdoing others by misguiding them.\nrefl\nأَمۡ يَقُولُونَ ٱفۡتَرَىٰهُۖ قُلۡ فَأۡتُواْ بِعَشۡرِ سُوَرٖ مِّثۡلِهِۦ مُفۡتَرَيَٰتٖ وَٱدۡعُواْ مَنِ ٱسۡتَطَعۡتُم مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ إِن كُنتُمۡ صَٰدِقِينَ ١٣\nAllah challenges them to produce the like of the Quran, saying, (Then let them produce a discourse like this) [52:34], and challenges them to produce (ten Suras like it) [11:13], but they could not do either. Then He challenges them to produce (one Surah like it) [10:38], and again they could not, and neither could anyone else among all created beings. Ibn Taimyah: 3/509.\nExplain the stages of the challenge presented to the disbelievers to produce the like of the Quran.\nقُلۡ فَأۡتُواْ بِعَشۡرِ سُوَرٖ مِّثۡلِهِۦ مُفۡتَرَيَٰتٖ وَٱدۡعُواْ مَنِ ٱسۡتَطَعۡتُم مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ إِن كُنتُمۡ صَٰدِقِينَ ١٣ فَإِلَّمۡ يَسۡتَجِيبُواْ لَكُمۡ فَٱعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّمَآ أُنزِلَ بِعِلۡمِ ٱللَّهِ\nThen Allah, the Exalted, explains the miracle of the Quran, and that no one is able to produce the like of it, or even bring ten Surahs, or (a Surah like it) [2:23]. That is because the Speech of the Lord is not like the speech of the created beings, just as His attributes are not like the attributes of the creation. Ibn Kathir: 2/420.\nNo one is able to produce the like of this Quran, why?\nفَٱعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّمَآ أُنزِلَ بِعِلۡمِ ٱللَّهِ وَأَن لَّآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَۖ\nThis also indicates that what we need to seek certain knowledge about, and not rely on mere conjecture, is the Quran and Tawhīd (Oneness of Allah), because Allah says: (Then know that it [the Quran] was revealed with the knowledge of Allah, and that there is no deity except Him). Al-Saadi: 378.\nWhat does the expression (Then know) indicate?\nمَن كَانَ يُرِيدُ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةَ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَزِينَتَهَا نُوَفِّ إِلَيۡهِمۡ أَعۡمَٰلَهُمۡ فِيهَا وَهُمۡ فِيهَا لَا يُبۡخَسُونَ ١٥\nMeaning: All their aspirations are limited to this worldly life and its adornments, such as women and sons, heaped-up hordes of gold and silver, fine horses, livestock and well-tilled land. Thus, they focus their ambitions, efforts and striving on these things, and they do not aspire to the Hereafter at all. Such a person can be nothing but a disbeliever because if he were a believer, his faith would have prevented him from focusing all his attention on this world. Al-Saadi: 379.\nHow can you infer that this verse pertains to the polytheists?\nمَن كَانَ يُرِيدُ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةَ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَزِينَتَهَا نُوَفِّ إِلَيۡهِمۡ أَعۡمَٰلَهُمۡ فِيهَا وَهُمۡ فِيهَا لَا يُبۡخَسُونَ ١٥ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَيۡسَ لَهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ إِلَّا ٱلنَّارُۖ وَحَبِطَ مَا صَنَعُواْ فِيهَا وَبَٰطِلٞ مَّا كَانُواْ يَعۡمَلُونَ ١٦\nIt is said that the meaning of this verse pertains to those who are ostentatious. It is narrated that on the Day of Resurrection, it will be said to them: \"You have fasted, prayed, gave for charity, participated in Jihad, and recited the Quran so that people would say so about you, and they did.\" Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"Those are the first people by whom the fire will be enflamed.\" This Hadith was narrated by Abu Huraira (t) who wept intensely...[Sahih Muslim]. Al-Qurtubi: 11/84.\nWhat will happen on the Day of Resurrection to those who show off their good deeds?\nأَفَمَن كَانَ عَلَىٰ بَيِّنَةٖ مِّن رَّبِّهِۦ وَيَتۡلُوهُ شَاهِدٞ مِّنۡهُ وَمِن قَبۡلِهِۦ كِتَٰبُ مُوسَىٰٓ إِمَامٗا وَرَحۡمَةًۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِهِۦۚ\nMeaning: Is one who relies on a clear proof from his Lord like one who seeks this worldly life and its adornment? Or, is one who relies on a clear proof from his Lord like one who is immersed in misguidance and ignorance. Al-Baghawi: 2/392.\nOne who is attached to this worldly life, and another whom Allah guided to the truth, Are they the same?\nأَلَا لَعۡنَةُ ٱللَّهِ عَلَى ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ١٨ ٱلَّذِينَ يَصُدُّونَ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ وَيَبۡغُونَهَا عِوَجٗا وَهُم بِٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ هُمۡ كَٰفِرُونَ ١٩\n(Those who avert) themselves and others from faith and obedience. (Seeking to make it crooked), they move people away from the right path to sins and shirk. Al-Qurtubi: 11/92.\nWhat are the traits of those who are cursed by Allah in this verse?\nwords\nلاَ يُبخَسُونَThey will not be deprived from the reward of this worldly life\nمِريَةٍDoubt\nالأَشهَادُThe angels, the Prophets, and human limbs that will testify on the Day of Resurrection\nوَيَبغُونَهَاThey want it [crooked]\nعِوَجًاCrooked, in accord with their whims"],[224,"§Hud\ndeeds\nPray two rak'as, then invoke Allah with humility to grant you humbleness to Him, which is modesty and submission to Him.\nShare a message in which you suggest three ways of inviting eminent people to Allah.\nDeliver a talk, give advice, or eliminate an evil with a nice approach; then read the narratives of Prophets in Surat Hud, for many aims of this Surah will be evident to you.\nguid\nMisguiding others is a cause for a multiplied punishment, so beware of leading others to commit a sin.\nWhen inviting others to Allah, do not disdain anyone for his low social or economic status.\nFocus on inviting eminent individuals since they can be a cause for the guidance of their followers.\nrefl\nيُضَٰعَفُ لَهُمُ ٱلۡعَذَابُۚ مَا كَانُواْ يَسۡتَطِيعُونَ ٱلسَّمۡعَ وَمَا كَانُواْ يُبۡصِرُونَ ٢٠\n(Their punishment will be multiplied), it will be intensified and increased because they went astray themselves and led others astray. Al-Saadi: 379.\nWhy will their punishment be multiplied?\nلَا جَرَمَ أَنَّهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ هُمُ ٱلۡأَخۡسَرُونَ ٢٢\nAllah explains that they are the biggest losers among mankind in their transaction for the abode of the Hereafter. That is because they exchanged the highest levels of Paradise for the lowest depths of Hellfire, and they substituted the pleasure of Gardens of Paradise for the fierce boiling water of Hellfire. They exchanged the drink of sealed nectar with the fierce hot wind, scalding water, and a shade of black smoke. They chose food from the filth of dirty wounds instead of wide-eyed lovely maidens. They preferred the abyss in Hellfire instead of lofty castles. They chose the wrath of Allah and His punishment over nearness to Him and the blessing of gazing at Him. Ibn Kathir: 2/423.\nAllah describes them as the worst losers, Why?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَأَخۡبَتُوٓاْ إِلَىٰ رَبِّهِمۡ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ أَصۡحَٰبُ ٱلۡجَنَّةِۖ هُمۡ فِيهَا خَٰلِدُونَ ٢٣\n(And humble themselves before their Lord), humbleness is humility due to fear in the heart. In Arabic, the word used for humbleness refers to a land with a flat surface. Humbleness is humility with serenity , or constant turning to Allah in repentance. Al-Qurtubi: 11/96.\nHow does the servant become among those who humble themselves before Allah?\nفَقَالَ ٱلۡمَلَأُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ مِن قَوۡمِهِۦ مَا نَرَىٰكَ إِلَّا بَشَرٗا مِّثۡلَنَا وَمَا نَرَىٰكَ ٱتَّبَعَكَ إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ أَرَاذِلُنَا بَادِيَ ٱلرَّأۡيِ وَمَا نَرَىٰ لَكُمۡ عَلَيۡنَا مِن فَضۡلِۢ بَلۡ نَظُنُّكُمۡ كَٰذِبِينَ ٢٧\nOur scholars said: The chiefs were more resistant to the Message because of their overwhelming love for headship, the difficulty of being detached from it and their pride which keeps them from following others. A poor individual has none of these obstacles, and so he responds to the Message and follows the Messenger. This is the typical way of most people in this worldly life. Al-Qurtubi: 11/99.\nTruth is more likely to be accepted by the poor, and rejected by the eminent rich. Why?\nفَقَالَ ٱلۡمَلَأُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ مِن قَوۡمِهِۦ مَا نَرَىٰكَ إِلَّا بَشَرٗا مِّثۡلَنَا وَمَا نَرَىٰكَ ٱتَّبَعَكَ إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ أَرَاذِلُنَا بَادِيَ ٱلرَّأۡيِ\nThis proved their ignorance since they criticized the Prophet (ﷺ) for being human, which is not really a flaw, because All Prophets (p) were sent with signs and proofs, and did not have to change the forms or images [of themselves or their followers]. They were sent to all people, and if a poor person accepts the Message, this would not affect them in a negative way since they have to accommodate all of their followers. Al-Qurtubi: 11/99.\nFor one who calls others to Allah, is having poor and destitute followers considered a shortcoming in his message?\nفَقَالَ ٱلۡمَلَأُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ مِن قَوۡمِهِۦ مَا نَرَىٰكَ إِلَّا بَشَرٗا مِّثۡلَنَا وَمَا نَرَىٰكَ ٱتَّبَعَكَ إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ أَرَاذِلُنَا بَادِيَ ٱلرَّأۡيِ وَمَا نَرَىٰ لَكُمۡ عَلَيۡنَا مِن فَضۡلِۢ بَلۡ نَظُنُّكُمۡ كَٰذِبِينَ ٢٧\n(The lowest among us), they described Noah's followers as (lowest) due to their poverty, thinking that honor is gained only through wealth, but that is far from the truth. In fact, despite their poverty, Noah's followers were more honorable than these chiefs. (Unwittingly), without thinking, which means that the lowest among us followed you without foresight or certainty. Ibn Juzay: 1/394.\nThis verse sheds light on the traits of disbelievers when they accuse the believers. Explain.\nقَالَ يَٰقَوۡمِ أَرَءَيۡتُمۡ إِن كُنتُ عَلَىٰ بَيِّنَةٖ مِّن رَّبِّي وَءَاتَىٰنِي رَحۡمَةٗ مِّنۡ عِندِهِۦ فَعُمِّيَتۡ عَلَيۡكُمۡ أَنُلۡزِمُكُمُوهَا وَأَنتُمۡ لَهَا كَٰرِهُونَ ٢٨\nThis is an allusion that if they had reflected objectively without hatred and enmity, they would have known that his Message was true. Ibn Ashur: 12/51.\nStubbornness and hatred influence the attitude of polytheists. Explain.\nwords\nمُعجِزِينَYou will not escape from Allah’s punishment\nوَأَخبَتُواThey humbled themselves\nأَرَاذِلُنَاThe lowest among us\nبَادِيَ الرَّأيِWithout thinking\nفَعُمِّيَت عَلَيكُمBut you fail to see it\nأَنُلزِمُكُمُوهَاCan we force you to accept it?"]])